## 8. Component Type Specs (Schema Validation)

### `model` type
```json
{
  "schema": "<CONFIG_REGISTRY_URL>",
  "framework": "pytorch",
  "task": "embedding",
  "size": "512",
  "baseModel": "my_component_id:my_version"
}
```
- Stored as `model.json` descriptor artifact
- Multiple unzipped files (weights, tokenizers, configs)
- Used by TEAMServe deployments

### `sagemaker-package` type
```json
{
  "schema": "<CONFIG_REGISTRY_URL>",
  "packages": ["model.tar.gz", "model2.tar.gz"]
}
```
- Stored as `sagemaker_package.json` descriptor
- Packages must be `.tar.gz` files
- Validator checks: descriptor present, artifacts exist, are tar.gz

### `prompt` type
- v1 schema (single-turn): `{schema, inference: {modelId, outputType, configuration}, prompt: {text, variables}}`
- v2 schema (multi-role chat): `{schema, inference: {...}, prompts: [{role, text, variables}]}`

**Sources:**
- [Component Specs](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/4629793961/Component+Specs)
- [Downstream-consumer integration cookbook](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020e8e542e6fbb547dea43317e50413b60f/pages/7086703166/Downstream-consumer+integration+cookbook)

