## 1. Platform Overview & Data Model

### What it is
Tarot v3 (also called "ML Registry v3") is Atlassian's **centralized ML artifact registry** — the single source of truth for ML/AI assets (models, prompts, datasets, modules, Sagemaker packages). It replaces the legacy v2 API (being removed June 30, 2026).

### How the Data Model Works
The v3 API uses a hierarchical entity model:

```
Namespace → Component (type + owner) → Version (group of artifacts) → Artifacts (files with metadata)
```

**Key entities:**
| Entity | Description | Key Properties |
|--------|-------------|----------------|
| **Namespace** | Organizational folder; can nest arbitrarily deep. | `name`, `description`, `owner` (AD group), permissions |
| **Component** | A logical ML asset with a type. | `id` (UUID), `name`, `type` (model, prompt, dataset, sagemaker-package, etc.), `owner`, permissions |
| **Version** | An immutable snapshot grouping artifacts. | `id` (auto-incremented per component), `description`, `labels[]`, `artifacts[]` |
| **Artifact** | An individual file uploaded to a component. | `id`, `filename`, `hash`, `size`, `classification`, `attribution` |
| **Tag** | A mutable alias pointing to a specific version. | e.g. `production`, `v1.2.0` |
| **Annotation** | Append-only metadata attached to a version (e.g. eval results). | `type`, `description`, `artifacts[]` |

**Sources:**
- [Nandini x Riteka Brain Dump](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120203d1d05da1ecb49d1a4596a19bb96d37b/pages/6635061712/Nandini+x+Riteka+Brain+Dump)
- [ML Registry - user guide](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/4594240174/ML+Registry+-+user+guide)
- [Tarot V3 Data Labelling](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/4836534532/Tarot+V3+Data+Labelling)

