# Research Findings: Blameless PIR / Postmortem Schemas for `pir_auto_drafter` Tool and `pir-drafting` Skill

## 1. TTD/TTH/TTR/TTC Metric Definitions

### What It Is
Atlassian's Post-Incident Review process uses four core operational time metrics (collectively "TTx metrics") to measure incident response performance. These are quantified from the incident timeline and have formal SLO targets.

### How It Works — Precise Definitions

| Metric | Full Name | Definition | Calculation Basis | SLO Target |
|--------|-----------|------------|-------------------|------------|
| **TTD** | Time to Detect | Duration from impact start to organizational awareness/acknowledgment of the problem | `Detection timestamp − Impact start timestamp` | < 30 minutes (previously<15 min for some teams) |
| **TTH** | Time to HOT | Interval from when Sev-2 impact was first reached to creation of the HOT (or upgrade to Sev-2) | `HOT creation time − Sev-2 breach time` OR `Sev-2 HOT upgrade time − Sev-2 breach time` | < 25 minutes |
| **TTM** | Time to Mitigate | Time from Sev-2 breach to when major impact halted (no longer Sev-2+) | `Mitigation timestamp − Sev-2 breach time` | < 2 hours |
| **TTR** | Time to Resolve | Time from detection to full resolution/remediation of customer impact | `Resolution timestamp − Detection timestamp` | < 2 hours |
| **TTC** | Time to Communicate | Elapsed time from HOT creation to first external communication to affected customers | `First external comms timestamp − HOT creation time` | < 30 minutes |

**Additional metric observed:**
- **TTE** (Time to Engage): Time for engineering team to begin investigating from detection time.

### How It Applies to `pir_auto_drafter`
The tool should:
1. Accept reasoning traces / incident timeline data and automatically compute TTD/TTH/TTR/TTM/TTC from timestamps
2. Compare computed values against SLO targets and generate pass/fail assessments
3. When a metric fails its SLO, auto-generate an action item linked to the appropriate "PIR - TTD Action" or "PIR - TTR Action" or "PIR - TTC Action" link type
4. Output the standard metrics checklist table format:

```
| Metric Type | Result |
|---|---|
| Detected by Monitoring? | Yes or No |
| TTD less than 30 minutes | Yes/No (If No → PIR - TTD Action) |
| TTH less than 25 minutes | Yes/No (If No → PIR - TTD Action) |
| TTM less than 2 hours | Yes/No (If No → PIR - TTR Action) |
| TTC less than 30 minutes | Yes/No (If No → PIR - TTC Action) |
| Incident with similar root cause in past12 months? | Yes/No |
| Root cause category filled accurately | Yes/No |
| Recovery by field filled accurately | Yes/No |
| Preventable by field filled accurately | Yes/No |
| Progressive rollout/change control followed? | Yes/No/NA |
```

### Sources
- [TEMPLATE: PIR (for automation only with LLM)](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IMPIR/pages/5157362446)
- [PIR Changes Required to Support TTx Metrics](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Spork/pages/5893427416)
- [My PIR Template SEV Review Template](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202073545c6b3cd948d4a746b418bcc3a60c/pages/4051865538)

