## 11. Industry Best Practices (External Frameworks)

### Google SRE Postmortem Philosophy
- Written record of events + root cause analysis + action items
- Expected after any undesirable event (not limited to outages)
- Triggers: user-visible downtime, data loss, on-call intervention, resolution time above threshold, monitoring failure
- Reviewed internally/externally, then shared broadly
- Postmortem of the month / reading clubs / Wheel of Misfortune practices

### ITIL Problem Management Integration
- Incident → Problem → Change flow
- If incident not detected by monitoring → auto-create problem record assigned to SRE team
- Pattern: ties incident → problem → action in automated way

### Atlassian Incident Handbook (Public Best Practice)
- Draft within 24-48 hours, no more than 5 business days
- Assign specific person familiar with incident
- Work from a template for consistency
- Include detailed timeline with specific times
- Capture incident metrics for trend analysis over time
- Review every PIR in recurring monthly meetings
- The "5Whys" technique for uncovering deep factors

