## 2. PIR Document Schema / Template Structure

### What It Is
The canonical Atlassian PIR structure comprises a Confluence document (qualitative narrative) paired with a Jira OpsJ PIR ticket (structured data). The full document has a well-defined section hierarchy.

### How It Works — Complete PIR Document Schema

```
1. METADATA
   - Date of PIR
   - Date of Review (must be within 72 hours)
   - Investigators / Authors
   - Incident Responders
   - PIR Champion
   - Interviews (if any)
   - Head of Engineering (mandatory pre-review/sign-off for Sev0/1)

2. INCIDENT SUMMARY
   - Executive TL;DR (2-3 sentences: timing, impact, root cause, learnings)
   - Customer/Service
   - Severity (with rationale)
   - Primary Impact

3. NARRATIVE
   - Context/background
   - Is this a recurrence?
   - Impact quantification (SLO/SLA impact)
   - Incident management effectiveness
   - Deployment and Testing
   - Support tickets
   - External/Internal Comms
   - Financial and Business Impact

4. SEVERITY CRITERIA
   - Severity matrix/factors
   - Artifacts reviewed
   - Correctness assessment

5. IMPACT
   - Customer impact (tenants, % traffic, key accounts)
   - Functional impact (symptoms)
   - Business impact (SLA breaches, revenue, trust)
   - Telemetry assessment score (1-10 scale)

6. TIMELINE (UTC, 24h format)
   - Impact Start Time
   - TTD marker (first alert)
   - Major Impact Breached
   - TTH marker (HOT creation)
   - TTC marker (first external comms)
   - TTM marker (mitigation)
   - TTR marker (full resolution)
   - Impact End

7. ROOT CAUSE / FIVE WHYS
   - Problem statement
   - Branching "Why" chains (RC, CC, SG classifications)
   - Stopping criteria: Root Cause found / Insufficient Data / Not Resolvable Organisationally
   - Cause types: RC (Root Cause), CC (Contributing Cause), SG (System Gap)

8. RESOLUTION
   - Current state (Resolved/Cancelled/Deferred)
   - Customer path forward

9. MITIGATORS
   - War room actions
   - Hypotheses tested

10. ACTIONS (with Jira ticket links)
    - Action Link Type: TTD / TTR / TTC / Critical / High / Medium / Low / Improvement / Risk
    - Priority / Owner / Owning Team / Action Item Summary
    - Each action must be: Specific, Bounded, Actionable

11. INCIDENT METRICS CHECKLIST (TTx table)

12. LESSONS
    - Observability gaps
    - Runbook/Playbook updates needed

13. PROCESS DIFFICULTIES

14. RISKS
    - Ongoing risks exposed by incident
    - Mitigation strategy

15. OTHER TEAMS ENGAGEMENT

16. WHERE WE GOT LUCKY

17. APPENDIX
    - Detailed analysis links
    - Linked Jira epics/tickets
    - Dashboard/data source links

18. FEEDBACK (link to feedback form)
```

### How It Applies
The `pir_auto_drafter` should:
- Accept incident timeline, Slack channel transcript, reasoning traces as input
- Auto-populate sections1-6, 10-11 from structured data
- Generate draft narrative (section 3) and root cause analysis (section 7) from reasoning traces
- Flag sections requiring human review (e.g., "Lessons", "Where We Got Lucky")
- Output both: Confluence page content AND structured Jira ticket fields

