## 4. Action Item Priority SLOs and Classification

### What It Is
PIR action items are Jira tickets linked to the parent PIR ticket with specific link types that determine their SLO tracking.

### How It Works

**Priority Levels and SLOs (current, as of July 2024reduction):**

| Priority | SLO Start Date | SLO Completion Date | Description |
|----------|---------------|--------------------|----|
| **Critical** | 1business day (from action creation) | 2 weeks (from incident resolution) | Ongoing risks requiring immediate attention; critical code flaws; interim playbooks |
| **High** | 3 business days (from action creation) | 4 weeks (from incident resolution) | Crucial tasks for availability, monitoring gaps, conditional code fixes, playbook updates |
| **Medium** | 1 week (from action creation) | 7 weeks (from incident resolution) | Monitoring enhancements, KB updates, code improvements supporting normal ops |
| **Low** | 4 weeks (from action creation) | 10 weeks (from incident resolution) | Training gaps, on-call roster improvements, vendor collaboration, DR replication |
| **Improvement** | No SLO tracking | No SLO | Low-risk/high-cost items; must reference an artifact |

**Risk/Cost Classification Matrix:**
| Risk / Cost | Low Cost | High Cost |
|-------------|----------|-----------|
| High Risk | High Priority | Medium Priority |
| Medium Risk | Medium Priority | Low Priority |
| Low Risk | Low Priority | Improvement Action |

**Special Action Link Types (tracked separately):**
- `PIR - TTD Action` — Actions to improve detection time
- `PIR - TTR Action` — Actions to improve resolution time
- `PIR - TTC Action` — Actions to improve communication time (starting Q2-FY26)
- Default SLO for TTD/TTR/TTC actions: 4 weeks from HOT resolution

**Action Item Quality Requirements:**
- Must be Specific (narrow scope)
- Must be Bounded (clear completion criteria)
- Must be Actionable (concrete, not vague)
- Each must be tied to a Jira ticket
- Must have an Owner and Owning Team

### How It Applies
The `pir_auto_drafter` should:
- Auto-classify proposed action items using the Risk/Cost matrix
- Compute SLO due dates from incident resolution date
- Generate action items in the standard table format
- Link TTD/TTR/TTC-specific actions to appropriate link types
- Validate action item quality (specific, bounded, actionable) before output
- Flag when "human confirmation required" for priority assignment in🟡 autonomy tier

