## Finding 2: V8 Action Tier Classification — Production Implementation Pattern

### What it is
A concrete, production-grade implementation of the 3-tier model with action-type registry, staging pipeline, and receipt system.

### How it works

**Action-type registry structure (TS/JSON):**
```typescript
interface ActionTypeRegistryEntry {
  action_type: string;           // e.g., "coaching.slack.send"
  tier: 1 | 2 | 3;
  decision_reasoning: {
    Q1_external_write: boolean;
    Q3_reversible: boolean;
    Q4_single_entity: boolean;
    Q5_external_comm: boolean;
  };
  reversibility_window: string | null;  // ISO8601 duration: "PT5M", "PT1H", null
  override: string | null;              // e.g., "confidence_floor"
}
```

**Concrete classification examples:**
| action_type | Tier | Reasoning | Reversibility |
|------------|------|-----------|---------------|
| coaching.slack.send | 3 | Q1 YES, Q3 NO, Q5 YES | null |
| coaching.meeting.schedule | 3 | Q1 YES, Q3 NO, Q5 YES | null |
| coaching.email.send (Gmail draft) | 1 | Q1 YES, Q3 NO, Q5 NO (draft, human must send) | PT24H |
| coaching.confluence.create (draft) | 1 | Draft only | PT24H |
| signal.acknowledged | 2 | Agent-staged action in ActState | PT1H |

**Staging pipeline behavior:**
- Tier 1: Pass-through, write receipt, no staging UI
- Tier 2: Stage with 5s default-commit window; user can abort; `action.aborted` emitted on cancel/timeout
- Tier 3: ImpactPreview confirmation component rendered; explicit click-through required before commit fires

**Migration rule:** "Every PR adding a new action_type must include the tier classification with reasoning. If during integration we discover an action has more downstream impact than initially classified, follow the spec migration pattern (promote, never rewrite historical receipts)."

**Per-action receipt schema:**
```
actor_id, action_type, trigger_id, session_id, entity_ref, entity_type, 
timestamp, context_json, consequence_tier, before_state, after_state, 
reasoning (if agent-initiated), reversibility_window
```

### How it applies

**For `deployment_manifest_generator` or `autonomy_tier_router`:**
- Implement an action-type registry as a versioned artifact
- Every classified action carries a reasoning trace documenting which decision-tree questions were evaluated
- Include a `tier-assertion test` per action_type ensuring classification doesn't drift
- Include a `reversibility test` per action_type ensuring undo mechanics work within window

**Source:** [V8 Pipeline Briefing — Action Tier Classification Map (Pilot Scope)](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ots2/pages/7086503722), [S360-8505](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/S360-8505), [S360-8503](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/S360-8503)

