## Finding 3: Agent Action Risk Tiering Guide — Organizational Classification

### What it is
A broader organizational framework for classifying AI-driven actions based on impact severity, scope, and governance requirements.

### How it works

| Tier | Name | Definition | Examples |
|------|------|-----------|----------|
| 🔴 **Tier 1** | High Risk (Critical & Irreversible) | Persistent or destructive "one-way door" decisions | Decommissioning cloud resources, modifying global permissions, executing wire transfers, mass customer communications |
| 🟡 **Tier 2** | Medium Risk (Segmented & Reversible) | Scoped "two-way door" actions within single project/user environment | Creating Jira projects/tickets, labeling/assigning intake, opening PRs with code fixes, summarizing Slack threads |
| 🟢 **Tier 3** (implied) | Low Risk (Read/Navigate) | Informational or navigational actions with no write side-effects | Reading data, generating summaries, internal drafts |

**Classification heuristics:**
1. **Reversibility** — Can the action be undone? One-way door vs two-way door
2. **Blast radius** — Single entity vs multi-project vs organization-wide
3. **External impact** — Internal-only vs customer-facing vs legal/financial
4. **Data sensitivity** — Public info vs PII vs regulated data

### How it applies

The `symphony-autonomy-policy` skill should encode these heuristics as a decision function the agent evaluates before every action:

```
classify(action) → {
  reversibility: "irreversible" | "soft_reversible" | "fully_reversible",
  blast_radius: "single_entity" | "project" | "org_wide" | "customer_facing",
  data_sensitivity: "public" | "internal" | "pii" | "regulated",
  external_impact: "none" | "internal_team" | "customer" | "legal_financial"
} → tier: 1 | 2 | 3
```

**Source:** [Agent Action Risk Tiering Guide](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202048b8a48354b248e5a7bc624a3cad12a4/pages/6762507962)

