## Finding 6: AI-Native Support Escalation Gradient (L0–L4)

### What it is
A confidence-based escalation framework where AI confidence determines the level of human involvement.

### How it works

| Level | Name | Confidence Threshold | Behavior |
|-------|------|---------------------|----------|
| **L0** | Auto |≥95% confidence | AI resolves, auto-sent |
| **L1** | Approve | 85–94% confidence | AI drafts, human approves |
| **L2** | Copilot | 70–84% confidence | Human leads, AI suggests |
| **L3** | Assist | <70% confidence | Human does, AI researches |
| **L4** | Manual | Policy override | HIPAA/policy override customers bypass AI entirely |

**Gating rules:**
- Risk/impact matrix governs which operations require human approval regardless of confidence
- HIPAA/policy override customers bypass AI entirely → L4
- "High-impact operations (delete site, change permissions) always require human approval"
- Continuous session handoff via internal comments

### How it applies

**For `autonomy_tier_router` — confidence-to-tier mapping:**
```
if confidence >= 0.95AND risk_class == "low" → Tier 1 (🟢 autonomous)
if confidence >= 0.85 AND risk_class in ["low", "medium"] → Tier 2 (🟡 confirm)
if confidence >= 0.70 → Tier 2 (🟡 confirm with reasoning)
if confidence < 0.70 → Tier 3 (🔴 escalate)
if policy_override(action) → Tier 3 (🔴 always escalate)
```

**Source:** [CSS & Sales Support AI Features Catalog](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/qszX4DeBJqT4/pages/6510249916), [AI-First Support Transformation Vision](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202056fd0320303d4140aabd4a9d3138668a/pages/6657839223)

