## Finding 13: Blast Radius Classification Framework

### What it is
A complementary reliability-risk axis used alongside the reversibility-based tier classification.

### How it works (from Extended Workflow Taxonomy)

| Risk Level | Name | Signals | Examples |
|-----------|------|---------|----------|
| **R0** | High Blast Radius (Critical) | Multi-region/multi-tenant impact; changes global control-plane/routing; disables safety rails | Global traffic routing, shared control-plane config, global credential rotation, disabling WAF/rate limiters |
| **R1** | Medium Blast Radius (Elevated) | Single product/region/cluster impact; breaks critical dependency for that scope | Single-region config change, DB schema modification, shared queue/cache changes for one service group |
| **R2** | Low Blast Radius (Localized) | Single tenant/host/component; limited customer impact; easy rollback | Single-tenant config, individual host restart, component-level change |

**Jira Admin Agent implementation:**

| Severity | Criteria | Agent Behavior |
|----------|----------|---------------|
| Low | 1context, 1 scheme, 1-2 projects, no workflow dependencies | Execute with brief summary |
| Medium | Multiple contexts/schemes, several projects, some dependencies | Execute with explicit confirmation step |
| High | Global context, many projects, workflow rules referencing field, system/required field | Report only — do not execute without explicit override |

### How it applies

**For `autonomy_tier_router` — incorporate blast_radius as a promotion signal:**
```
if blast_radius == R0 → minimum Tier 3 (always escalate)
if blast_radius == R1 → minimum Tier 2 (always confirm)
if blast_radius == R2 → follow standard decision tree
```

**Source:** [Extended Workflow Taxonomy](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/acf/pages/6485187265), [Jira Admin Agent (EAP) - Field Operations & Blast Radius](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AG/pages/7075506774)

