## Finding 4: RFC-002 AI SDLC Governance Framework — L0–L5 Maturity Levels

### What it is
The canonical Atlassian maturity model for AI-driven workflows, assessed **per workflow per team**.

### How it works

| Level | Name | AI Role | Human Decision Authority | Typical Pattern |
|-------|------|---------|-------------------------|----------------|
| **L0** | No meaningful AI involvement | Absent or incidental | Humans perform all work and approvals | Manual workflow |
| **L1** | Assistive | Suggests or drafts | Humans review all outputs before use | Copilot-style support |
| **L2** | Structured assistance | Performs bounded tasks with workflow integration | Humans retain explicit approval on every action | Integrated recommendations with audit trail |
| **L3** | Conditional autonomy | Executes or adjudicates in low-risk cases | Humans oversee exceptions and sampled outcomes | Automation within risk and policy guardrails |
| **L4** | High autonomy | Handles most in-scope tasks autonomously | Humans govern policy, thresholds, and incident response | Autonomous operation with strong monitoring |
| **L5** | Near-full autonomy | Operates as primary decision-maker for eligible work | Humans provide governance, audits, and emergency intervention | Highly trusted closed-loop system |

**Design principles:**
1. **Composable by domain** — assessed independently per SDLC domain (code review, testing, deployment, etc.)
2. **Risk-bounded autonomy** — AI authority capped by risk profile of work being performed
3. **Evidence-based progression** — advancement requires observable evidence (concordance with human judgment, calibrated confidence, acceptable failure rates, sufficient coverage, operational feedback loops)
4. **No single aggregate score** — profiles across domains, not blended readiness numbers

**Readiness levels (prerequisite axis):**
- R0 (Not Ready) → R1 (Foundational) → R2 (Enabled) → R3 (Optimized)
- **Maturity is capped by Readiness** — e.g., R1 readiness caps maturity at L2

**Key constraint:** "Higher-risk situations require stronger controls, more evidence, and in some cases permanent human approval requirements."

### How it applies

**For the `symphony-autonomy-policy` skill — level promotion gate criteria:**

| Promotion | Required Evidence |
|-----------|------------------|
| L0 → L1 | Tool access configured; agent can suggest/draft; human reviews100% |
| L1 → L2 | Consistent context engineering; audit traces captured; reinforcement signal visibility |
| L2 → L3 | Human-in-the-loop approval rate tracked; concordance with human judgment demonstrated; failure rate at or below human baseline;4-6 weeks sustained operation |
| L3 → L4 | Formal evidence review under RFC-002 gates; failure rate parity with human performance; 8+ weeks sustained; strong monitoring and anomaly detection |
| L4 → L5 | Incident feedback loop operational; correlated failure rate acceptably low; mature risk engine; runtime containment proven |

**Source:** [RFC-002 - AI SDLC Governance Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AISDLC/pages/6849219616), [Core Eng AI Maturity Model — V1](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CoreEngineering/pages/7046656407)

