## Finding 9: Code Review AI Maturity Model (L0–L5) — Evidence-Based Progression Gates

### What it is
A detailed6-level model specifically for AI-driven code review/approval that provides the most concrete gate-to-gate evidence requirements.

### How it works

| Level | Approval Mechanism | What Agents Approve | Human Role | Key Gate to Next |
|-------|-------------------|--------------------| -----------|-----------------|
| L0: Manual | Human judgment | Nothing | Review everything | Traceability infrastructure |
| L1: Assisted | Human + CI | Nothing | Review all real changes | Risk classification + AI reviewer + canary |
| L2: Low-risk | AI reviewer + policy + CI | Docs, refactors, dep bumps | Review medium + high risk | Executable policy + specialized reviewers |
| L3: Medium-risk | Evidence thresholds + specialized agents | Non-critical logic, bounded features | Review exceptions + high risk | Differential testing + validated rollback |
| L4: Conditional high | Evidence + runtime containment | High-scrutiny with strong reversibility | Review ambiguous/sensitive | Mature risk engine + incident feedback |
| L5: Default machine | Policy-governed approval | Most changes within policy | Govern policy + handle exceptions | — |

**Critical framing:** "The key question at each level is not 'are our models good enough?' but 'have we built enough policy, evidence, containment, and accountability to make human review unnecessary for this class of change?'"

**Gate requirements for L2→L3:**
- Risk classification system operational
- Change manifests in use
- AI review agent deployed and calibrated
- Canary/rollback infrastructure proven
- Measurement: failure rates of AI-approved changes vs human-approved changes

**Gate requirements for L3→L4:**
- Differential testing against prior behavior
- Synthetic replay in staging environments
- Validated rollback mechanisms (tested, not theoretical)
- Policy-aware deployment orchestration
- Anomaly-triggered automatic rollback
- Explicit escalation rules for ambiguity and weak evidence

### How it applies

**For the maturity assessment in `day-one-readiness-bootstrap`:**
- New AI employee starts at L0-L1
- Progression to L2 requires: audit trail, structured context, basic policy checks
- "Expand autonomy only when the data shows the system catches problems at least as well as humans did"
- Duration gates recommended: 4-6 weeks for L2→L3, 8+ weeks for L3→L4

**Source:** [A Maturity Model for AI in Code Review](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~cknott/pages/6677006234)

