## 3. REST API Endpoints — Complete Surface

### 3.1 Metrics Ingestion API

**`POST /api/v1/metrics`** — Ingest metrics

```json
{
  "timestamp": "2025-08-06T20:13:05Z",
  "reference_id": "uuid12321",
  "metric_namespace": "confluence",
  "metrics": [
    {
      "metric_key": "row_count_for_confluence_page",
      "type": "number",
      "value": 1000,
      "tags": {
        "subproject": "ranking",
        "tenant_id": "uuid-abc"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

**Response**: `200 OK`

**Key constraints:**
- `metric_namespace` must contain at least one `.` separator (e.g., `namespace.evaluation_metric.mean`)
- `type` enum: `number`, `boolean`, `string`
- First emission of a metric key locks the type; subsequent emissions with different type are rejected
- Tags passed as flat JSON object (key-value pairs)
- Certain tags (`model_id`, `tenant_id`, `product`, `region`) are promoted to top-level StarRocks columns

**Source**: [ML Lens Metrics API](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5806815768/ML+Lens+Metrics+API)

### 3.2 Data Quality / Profiling Runs API

**`POST /api/v1/run`** — Register a validation run

```json
{
  "environment": "prod",
  "namespace": "abc"
}
```
**Response**: `{ "run_id": "generated-uuid" }`

**`POST /api/v1/runs/metrics`** — Publish metrics for a run

```json
{
  "run_id": "generated-uuid",
  "namespace": "abc",
  "metrics": [
    {
      "metric_key": "null_count_col_A",
      "type": "number",
      "value": 42
    }
  ]
}
```

**Source**: [RFC: ML Lens API for data profile and data quality SDK integration](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5626083662)

### 3.3 Query API

**`POST /api/v1/observo/query/ai-event`** — Execute SQL queries against StarRocks

```json
{
  "query": "SELECT namespace, metric_key, numeric_value, timestamp FROM ai_events_v2 WHERE namespace = 'feature_observability.drift.ks_d' AND timestamp >= '2026-05-01' AND timestamp <= '2026-05-26'"
}
```

This is the ML Lens Query API that the drift computation jobs use over HTTP. Also exposed via direct Slauth curl:

```bash
atlas slauth curl -a ml-lens -e prod -- \
  -X POST "${BASE_URL}/api/v1/observo/query/ai-event" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"query": "SELECT ..."}'
```

**Source**: [Observo/Starrocks vs MLS Spike](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6514084136)

### 3.4 Aggregated Metrics Query

**`GET /api/v1/metrics/aggregated-analysis/{namespace.key}`** — Pre-aggregated metrics with filtering/dedup

Being extended with `MlLensClient.get_aggregated_metric()` SDK method.

**Source**: [Per-Tenant Model Regression Check Module](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202081bd6f4139e2470180dbbcb6c378ec78/pages/7062057973)

### 3.5 Alert Registration API (V1— Current Production)

**`POST /api/v1/alerts/register`** — Register alert configuration

```json
{
  "alert_key": "drift_alert",
  "alert_namespace": "feature_observability.drift",
  "alert_configs": [
    {
      "reference_period": {
        "type": "relative",
        "duration": "-2w"
      },
      "metric_namespace": "feature_observability.drift.ks_pvalue",
      "tag_filters": [
        { "key": "feature_service", "operator": "=", "value": "fraud_detection_v2" }
      ],
      "alert_conditions": [
        {
          "type": "single",
          "condition": {
            "measure": "expected_value",
            "operator": "<=",
            "value": 0.05
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "alert_message": "Drift detected in feature distributions.",
  "runbook": "https://...",
  "recipients": [
    { "type": "slack", "values": ["#ml-alerts"] },
    { "type": "jsm_ops", "values": ["eng-ml-platform"] }
  ]
}
```

**`GET /api/v1/alerts/<alertkey>?namespace=<namespace>`** — Retrieve alert config

**`DELETE /api/v1/alerts/<metricKey>?namespace=<namespace>`** — Delete alert config (requires admin group)

**Source**: [ML Lens Metrics API](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5806815768), [ML Lens Alerting Requirements](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5989280688)

### 3.6 Alert Rules V2 API (New — Observo-backed, in acceptance testing May 2026)

**`POST /api/v1/alerts/rules-v2`** — Create V2 alert rule

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| name | string | Yes | Human-readable name |
| useCase | string | Yes | Use-case identifier (e.g., `ml-lens`) |
| enabled | boolean | Yes | Active flag |
| alertConfig | array | Yes | List of alert config entries (filters, window, conditions) |
| alertMessage | string | No | Alert message text |
| responders | array | No | Responder targets |
| tags | array | No | String tags |
| extraProperties | object | No | Arbitrary metadata |

**GET/UPDATE/DELETE** use column-name query params for filtering. Pagination: `page` (0-based), `size` (default: 20, max: 100).

**Source**: [Alert Rule V2 - API Design](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/oi2/pages/6849148300)

