## 4. Drift Detection — Metrics & Algorithms

### 4.1 Supported Drift Metrics

| Metric Namespace | Algorithm | Feature Type | Output |
|-----------------|-----------|--------------|--------|
| `feature_observability.drift.ks_d` | Kolmogorov-Smirnov statistic | Numeric | Float0–1 |
| `feature_observability.drift.ks_pvalue` | KS test p-value | Numeric | Float 0–1 |
| `feature_observability.drift.psi` | Population Stability Index | Numeric/Categorical | Float ≥ 0 |
| `feature_observability.drift.chi_squared` | Chi-squared test | Categorical | Float |
| `feature_observability.drift.hellinger` | Hellinger distance | Numeric | Float 0–1 |

### 4.2 Drift Computation Approaches (DACI Decision: Option 2approved)

**Approved architecture**: ML Lens orchestrates drift computation via ML Studio Databricks jobs:
1. ML Lens scheduler triggers on cadence (Cronman / Quartz)
2. Config loaded from Postgres (reference window, baseline, thresholds)
3. Blueprint constructed and MLS job triggered
4. MLS job fetches feature data from StarRocks via ML Lens Query API (HTTP GET)
5. KS/PSI computed in Python/PySpark (scipy, numpy)
6. Results emitted back to ML Lens via Metrics API
7. Alert evaluation runs natively in ML Lens

**Alternative (Option 1 — StarRocks native)**: KS computed as `max(|Δquantile|)` over 100 quantile pairs directly in Kotlin. PSI/Hellinger via SQL aggregation with stored bin edges.

**Source**: [DACI: MLS vs ML Lens Drift Computation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6858051319), [Design: ML Lens Platform Data Drift Detection](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6738511349)

### 4.3 Reference Window Configuration

- **Sliding (default)**: 28-day lookback from current window
- **Fixed period**: Absolute start/end timestamps (e.g., `2025-09-01` to `2025-09-30`)
- **User-supplied baseline**: Summary stats (mean, stddev, min, max) provided directly

### 4.4 ML Data Quality SDK (Python)

```python
from atlassian_ml_dq_sdk.metrics.distribution import PopulationStabilityIndex, KolmogorovSmirnov, KLDivergence

# PSI
psi = PopulationStabilityIndex("feature_col", reference_distribution, bins=10)
psi_value = psi.compute(df)

# KS
ks = KolmogorovSmirnov("feature_col", reference_sample)
ks_stat, ks_pvalue = ks.compute(df)

# KL Divergence
kl = KLDivergence("feature_col", reference_distribution, bins=10)
kl_value = kl.compute(df)
```

Available metrics: `PopulationStabilityIndex`, `KLDivergence`, `KolmogorovSmirnov`, `FeatureDrift` (mean absolute bin frequency difference).

**Source**: [Drift Detection Metrics](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/6192530763), [ML Data Quality SDK](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/6192433232)

