## Finding 3: Risk Classification Schemas for Deployments

### What it is
Multiple risk classification frameworks used at Atlassian to determine deployment speed, soak times, and approval requirements.

### How it works

#### A. Spinnaker Risk Levels (Label-based)
| Risk Level | Soak Time (All Envs) | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `[high-risk]` | 1 day | Platform-level changes, affects all/many services or users |
| `[medium-risk]` | 2 hours | Usecase-level changes, won't bring down whole system |
| `[low-risk]` | 1 hour | Minor bug fixes, copy changes, thoroughly tested |
| `[skip-to-prod]` | 0 | Critical hotfix, overrides all other labels |
| `[no-soak]` | 0 | No risk (README updates) |

#### B. PR Risk Matrix (Impact × Complexity)
| Impact↓ / Complexity → | Low | Medium | High |
|---|---|---|---|
| **High Impact** | Medium | High | High |
| **Medium Impact** | Low | Medium | High |
| **Low Impact** | Low | Low | Medium |

**Impact factors**: How noticeable, SLA capability affected, breaking contract changes, detectability, effort to reverse, negative consequences of reversal
**Complexity factors**: Components affected, dependencies, verifiable in pre-prod

#### C. What constitutes "High Risk" (Bitbucket Change Management):
- Not easily roll back/forward-able
- Permanently alters customer data
- Schema migrations
- Modifying auto-scaling rules
- High blast radius (affects all/many services or users)
- Multi-team implementation

#### D. AI-Driven Change Risk Assessment (JSM):
- **Automated risk scoring**: 0-100 scale with Low/Medium/High classification
- **Four risk dimensions**: Technical, Operational, Security & Compliance, Business
- **Data sources**: Jira, Risk Insights, Bitbucket, Assets, Compass
- **Outputs**: Score, classification, mitigation recommendations, deduplication against approved playbook steps

#### E. Service Tier System:
- Tier 0: Critical backbone (AWS, Micros, DNS)
- Tier 1: Essential services (hot-escalation, Spinnaker)
- Tier 2: Non-core (Bamboo)
- Tier 3: Internal/non-critical

### How it applies
The `deployment_manifest_generator` tool should:
1. Auto-derive risk classification from: files changed (blast radius), service tier, dependencies touched, presence of schema migrations, data mutability
2. Map risk to deployment strategy: soak times, progressive rollout speed, approval requirements
3. Output both a numeric score (0-100) and categorical level (Low/Medium/High/Critical)

For the skill: The AI agent should autonomously generate the risk classification (🟢) but escalate to human confirmation (🟡) when risk≥ High.

### Source
- [Xflow: Spinnaker Risk Levels](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DISC/pages/3757227947/Xflow+Spinnaker+Risk+Levels)
- [AX Contribution PR Risk Matrix](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Growth/pages/5968636949/AX+Contribution+PR+Risk+Matrix)
- [Change Management Best Practices](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BB/pages/567911492/Change+Management+Best+Practices)
- [AI-Driven Change Risk Assessment](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020f8645f9b46414d32962ab94d66c30436/pages/6439063326/AI-Driven+Change+Risk+Assessment+Capabilities+Overview)

