## Autonomy Classification for Skill Design

| Manifest Section | Autonomy Tier | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Intent (from PR/Jira) | 🟢 Auto-generate | Derived from existing metadata |
| Non-goals | 🟡 Human review | Requires domain understanding of what's NOT in scope |
| Files/Services affected | 🟢 Auto-derive | From git diff and service graph |
| Invariants | 🟡 Human review + auto-suggest | Agent proposes from SLOs; human confirms |
| Risk classification | 🟢 Auto-score,🟡 if≥ High | Computed from heuristics; escalate high risk |
| Test plan status | 🟢 Auto-populate | From CI system |
| Rollback plan | 🟢 Auto-generate for Category 1,🟡 for Category 2/3 | Simple rollbacks are automated; complex ones need review |
| Deployment strategy | 🟢 for standard, 🔴 for non-standard | Standard follows SRM template; deviations need approval |
| Post-deploy monitoring | 🟢 Auto-populate | From existing PDV/dashboard config |
| Communication | 🟢 Auto-generate | Template-based |
| Authorization/Approval | 🔴 Always human | Policy requirement |

