## 9. Communication Tone & Format Guidelines per Cadence

### What It Is
Prescriptive guidance on tone, length, and format for each cadence tier — critical for an AI employee generating these communications autonomously.

### How It Works

| Cadence | Max Length | Tone | Format | Key Principles |
|---------|-----------|------|--------|----------------|
| **Continuous (alerts)** | 2-3 sentences | Urgent, factual | Slack message | State what happened, impact, action needed |
| **Per-experiment** | 1 page | Analytical, data-driven | Confluence page or Slack thread | Lead with recommendation, support with data |
| **Per-incident** | 3-5 sentences per update | Calm, transparent, reassuring | Statuspage + Slack | Acknowledge → identify → reassure → resolve |
| **Daily** | 3bullets per person | Concise, action-oriented | Standup format | Priorities, progress, problems |
| **Weekly** | <10 min read | Informative, high-signal | Structured digest | Wins, flags, escalations, FYIs |
| **Monthly** | 2-3 pages | Trend-focused, analytical | Report with charts | What changed, why, what's next |
| **Quarterly** | 5-7 pages | Strategic, outcome-focused | Executive report | ROI, portfolio health, strategic recommendations |

**Key Format Rules (from Atlassian Weekly Digest patterns):**
- Brief, high-signal updates (wins🏆, flags ⚠️, escalations 🔴, FYIℹ️)
- Links that quickly illustrate relevant work (Loom <1m, screenshots, Figma)
- Each digest consumable in <10 minutes
- Actions/Asks clearly separated from information

### How It Applies
The `stakeholder-communication-cadence` skill should encode these as tone/format constraints that the AI employee applies when generating any communication artifact. The `calibrated_uncertainty_reporter` tool applies specifically to the analytical tones (per-experiment, monthly, quarterly) where confidence levels matter.

