## 1. Communication Cadence Tier Framework

### What It Is
A structured multi-tier cadence model that ensures the right stakeholders receive the right information at the right frequency — ranging from continuous (event-driven) to quarterly (strategic). For ML teams specifically, these cadences map to ML lifecycle events rather than generic project milestones.

### How It Works — The7-Tier ML Communication Cadence

| Tier | Cadence | Trigger Source | Primary Audience | Content Type |
|------|---------|---------------|-----------------|--------------|
| **Continuous** | Event-driven (real-time) | ML Registry StreamHub events, SignalFx alerts, pipeline failures | On-call engineers, model owners | Alerts, drift notifications, deployment status |
| **Per-Experiment** | Experiment lifecycle (start→analyze→decide) | MLflow run completion, Statsig exposure targets hit | Experiment owner, DS lead, PM | Experiment results packet, go/no-go recommendation |
| **Per-Incident** | Incident lifecycle (detect→mitigate→resolve→PIR) | JSM Ops alerts, SLO breaches | Incident responders, stakeholders, affected teams | Incident status updates, PIR |
| **Daily** | Every workday | Scheduled (standup cadence) | Direct team | Priorities, progress, blockers |
| **Weekly** | Every Monday/Friday | Scheduled + aggregated events | Engineering manager, tech lead, adjacent teams | Experiment digest, operational health, sprint progress |
| **Monthly** | End of month | Aggregated metrics | Director/VP, product leadership | Model performance trends, cost attribution, business impact |
| **Quarterly** | End of quarter | OKR cycle | Executive leadership, cross-functional stakeholders | Strategic review, model portfolio health, ROI |

### How It Applies
The `stakeholder-communication-cadence` skill should encode these tiers as workflow steps, with the AI employee selecting the appropriate cadence based on the event type. The `weekly_experiment_digest` tool generates the weekly tier, while `escalation_router` handles routing between tiers (e.g., promoting a per-experiment finding to a weekly digest summary, or escalating an incident update to leadership).

