## 5. Quarterly ML Portfolio Review Report

### What It Is
A strategic-level report that synthesizes model portfolio health, experiment velocity, cost efficiency, and business impact for executive stakeholders. Generated quarterly to align with OKR cycles.

### How It Works

**Quarterly Report Structure:**

```markdown
# ML Portfolio Quarterly Review — [Team] — [Quarter]

## Executive Summary
[2-3 sentences: overall health, key wins, critical risks]

## 📈Experiment Velocity
- Experiments launched: [N]
- Experiments concluded: [M]
- Ship rate: [%]
- Average time-to-decision: [days]

## 🏥 Model Health Dashboard
| Model | Precision | Recall | Latency P90 | SLO Status | Last Retrained |
|-------|-----------|--------|-------------|------------|----------------|
| [from ML Lens quarterly aggregation] |

## 🔄 Lifecycle Events
- Models promoted to production: [N]
- Models retired: [M]
- Retraining events: [K] (scheduled: [X], drift-triggered: [Y])

## 💰 Cost & ROI
- Total ML compute spend: $[X] (Δ% vs last quarter)
- Cost per prediction: $[Y]
- Business value generated: [metric] (e.g., revenue uplift, cost savings)
- Notable: [TEAMServe migration savings, spot instance optimization]

## ⚠️ Risks & Debt
- Models approaching staleness threshold: [list]
- Unresolved PIR actions: [count]
- SLO breaches this quarter: [count, duration]

## 🎯 Next Quarter Priorities
- [derived from OKR planning]
```

### How It Applies
This is produced by the `weekly_experiment_digest` tool in "quarterly rollup" mode, aggregating 12-13 weekly digests plus additional strategic context. The AI employee drafts this and routes for human review (🟡 autonomy tier — it may influence planning decisions).

