## 6. Auto-Generation Architecture: Event-Driven Digest Pipeline

### What It Is
The technical architecture for auto-generating communication artifacts from ML lifecycle events, eliminating manual report compilation.

### How It Works

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                EVENT SOURCES│
├──────────────┬──────────────┬───────────────────────────┤
│ ML Registry  │ MLflow/ML│ Operational│
│ (StreamHub)  │ Studio       │ (SignalFx/JSM)            │
│              │              │                           │
│ • version│ • run        │ • SLO breach alerts       │
│   created    │   complete│ • pipeline failures       │
│ • artifact   │ • metric     │ • drift detections        │
│   uploaded   │   logged     │ • incident lifecycle      │
│ • deployment │ • stage      │ • cost anomalies          │
│   status     │   transition │                           │
└──────┬───────┴──────┬───────┴───────────┬───────────────┘
       │              │                   │
       ▼              ▼                   ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│EVENT AGGREGATION LAYER                      │
│(Scheduled job: daily/weekly/quarterly windows)          │
││
│  • Group events by time window│
│  • Enrich with context (model name, owner, team)         │
│  • Compute deltas (vs previous period)                   │
│  • Flag anomalies and attention items│
└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┘
                           │
                           ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              DIGEST GENERATION                │
│                                                          │
│  • Select template (daily/weekly/quarterly/incident)     │
│  • Populate with aggregated data                         │
│  • Apply audience-specific filtering                     │
│  • Generate natural-language summaries                   │
│  • Attach links to dashboards/artifacts                  │
└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┘
                           │
                           ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              DISTRIBUTION│
│                                                          │
│  • Slack channel post (weekly digest)                    │
│  • Confluence page creation (quarterly review)           │
│  • Email digest (monthly for leadership)                 │
│  • Jira comment (per-experiment decision record)         │
│  • Statuspage update (incident communication)            │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Key Design Principles:**
1. **Byproduct, not burden** — Communication is generated from events that already happen (model registration, experiment runs, alerts), not from manual data entry
2. **Progressive summarization** — Daily events roll up into weekly digests, which roll up into monthly/quarterly reports
3. **Audience-appropriate detail** — Engineers get metrics and links; leadership gets trends and decisions
4. **Idempotent and auditable** — Each digest links back to source events for traceability

### How It Applies
The `weekly_experiment_digest` tool implements the weekly generation step. The `escalation_router` handles real-time event routing (incidents, critical alerts). The `stakeholder-communication-cadence` skill provides the workflow guidance for when to generate what, for whom.

