## 7. Stakeholder Mapping for ML Teams

### What It Is
A framework for mapping ML team stakeholders to appropriate communication cadences and content levels.

### How It Works

| Stakeholder | Cadence | Content Level | Channel | What They Care About |
|-------------|---------|---------------|---------|---------------------|
| **Model Owner (MLE/DS)** | Continuous + Daily | Full technical detail | Slack alerts, dashboard | Metrics, drift, pipeline health |
| **Tech Lead /EM** | Daily + Weekly | Technical summary | Standup, weekly digest | Experiment velocity, blockers, team health |
| **Product Manager** | Per-experiment + Weekly | Business impact | Experiment packets, digest | Feature impact, ship decisions, timelines |
| **Director/VP Engineering** | Weekly + Monthly | Trends and risks | Digest summary, monthly review | Model portfolio health, cost, headcount efficiency |
| **Executive (C-level)** | Quarterly | Strategic outcomes | Quarterly review | ROI, competitive position, risk exposure |
| **Adjacent Teams (Platform, SRE)** | Per-incident + Weekly | Operational context | Incident channels, FYI section of digest | Dependencies, SLO impact, capacity needs |
| **Compliance/Legal** | Per-deployment + Quarterly | Audit trail | Deployment manifests, compliance reports | Data governance, model lineage, approval gates |

### How It Applies
The `escalation_router` uses this mapping to determine distribution lists. The `stakeholder-communication-cadence` skill encodes these mappings as configuration the AI employee consults when generating any communication.

