## 5. SignalFx REST API v2: Direct Detector CRUD

### 5.1 Endpoints

| Operation | Method | Endpoint |
|-----------|--------|----------|
| Create detector | `POST` | `https://api.{REALM}.signalfx.com/v2/detector` |
| Get detector | `GET` | `https://api.{REALM}.signalfx.com/v2/detector/{DETECTOR_ID}` |
| Update detector | `PUT` | `https://api.{REALM}.signalfx.com/v2/detector/{DETECTOR_ID}` |
| Delete detector | `DELETE` | `https://api.{REALM}.signalfx.com/v2/detector/{DETECTOR_ID}` |
| Search detectors | `GET` | `https://api.{REALM}.signalfx.com/v2/detector?name=...&limit=...&offset=...` |
| Preflight (preview) | `POST` | `https://api.{REALM}.signalfx.com/v2/signalflow/preflight` |
| Execute SignalFlow | `POST` | `https://api.{REALM}.signalfx.com/v2/signalflow/execute` |

Default realm at Atlassian: `us1`

### 5.2 Authentication

```
X-SF-TOKEN: <access_token>
```

Two token types:
- **User API Access Token**: Personal,30-day lifetime, from `go/sfx` → Profile → Settings
- **Org Token**: Service-level, managed by Sauron/Observability team

### 5.3Detector JSON Structure (REST API)

```json
{
  "name": "My Detector Name",
  "description": "Description of what this monitors",
  "programText": "A = data('metric').sum().publish(label='A')\ndetect(when(A > 100)).publish('Alert')",
  "rules": [
    {
      "detectLabel": "Alert",
      "severity": "Critical",
      "description": "High error rate detected",
      "disabled": false,
      "notifications": [
        {
          "type": "OpsGenie",
          "credentialId": "D2c_4qUA4AA",
          "responderId": "team-id",
          "responderName": "My Team",
          "responderType": "team"
        },
        {
          "type": "Slack",
          "credentialId": "DxJ_pZzA0N0",
          "channel": "my-alerts-channel"
        }
      ],
      "parameterizedSubject": "{{ruleSeverity}} Alert: {{{ruleName}}} ({{{detectorName}}})",
      "parameterizedBody": "...",
      "runbookUrl": "https://..."
    }
  ],
  "teams": ["team-id-1"],
  "tags": ["service:responsible-ai-api"]
}
```

### 5.4 Rate Limits for API

-1,200 jobs started per minute (org-wide, includes any SignalFlow execution)
- API calls subject to standard REST rate limits (undocumented exact number, but ~100 req/min per token is safe)

### 5.5 How This Applies to Tool Design

For the `signalfx_detector_client` wrapper:
- **Prefer Terraform over direct API** for create/update (leverages Sauron state management)
- Use REST API for **read-only operations**: list detectors, get detector status, validate existence
- Use the `/v2/signalflow/preflight` endpoint for **dry-run validation** of detector programs
- Use `/v2/signalflow/execute` for **backtesting** SignalFlow against historical data
- Auth: use sLauth token exchange or User API token from environment

**Source**: [Using SignalFX API to visualize detector status](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CCCR/pages/2706664159), [HOWTO: Subscribe to SignalFx notifications through terminal](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020f0d6f6ab90e4429898498a911b9af04d/pages/6676460603)

