## 6. Established Detector Type Patterns (Reusable Modules)

### 6.1 Standard Detector Types (from kt-signalfx-configuration)

| Detector Type | Module Path | Use Case |
|--------------|-------------|----------|
| `static-threshold-detector` | `detector-types/static-threshold-detector/` | Simple threshold-based alerts |
| `anomaly-detector` | `detector-types/anomaly-detector/` | Detects anomalous behavior |
| `multiburn-multiwindow-slo-alert` | `detector-types/multiburn-multiwindow-slo-alert/` | SLO-based alerts |
| `spring-boot-detectors` | `detector-types/spring-boot-detectors/` | Spring Boot metrics |
| `resilience4j-detectors` | `detector-types/resilience4j-detectors/` | Circuit breaker metrics |
| `sqs-client-detectors` | `detector-types/sqs-client-detectors/` | SQS queue monitoring |

### 6.2 Pattern: Static Threshold Module

```hcl
# static-threshold-detector/main.tf
resource "signalfx_detector" "static_threshold_detector" {
  name= var.name
  teams = [var.signalfx_team_id]

  program_text = <<-EOF
    A = data('${var.data_stream}',filter=${var.filter} and filter('micros_service_id', '${var.micros_service_id}'),
             rollup='sum')
        .sum()
        .publish(label='A')
    detect(when(A > threshold(${var.threshold}), lasting='${var.lasting}'))
      .publish('${var.detector_label}')
  EOF

  rule {
    detect_label  = var.detector_label
    severity      = var.severity
    notifications = var.notifications
    runbook_url   = var.runbook_url
    tip           = var.tip
    description   = var.description
  }
}
```

### 6.3 Pattern: Dynamic Detector with `for_each`

For creating multiple detectors from a map:

```hcl
resource "signalfx_detector" "per_integration_reliability" {
  for_each = var.integration_id_entity_type_list
  name     = "${var.resource_name_prefix}High Failure Rate - ${each.key}"
  
  program_text = <<-EOT
    failed = data('service.requests.count',filter=filter('integration_id', '${each.value[0]}')
                         and filter('result', 'failure'),
                  rollup='sum').sum(by=['environment', 'integration_id'])
             .publish(label='failed')
    
    total = (failed + successful).publish(label='total')
    failure_rate = (failed/total * 100).publish(label='failure_rate')
    
    detect(when(failure_rate > threshold(${var.thresholds[each.key]}), lasting='30m')and when(total > 200, lasting='30m'))
      .publish('High Failure Rate for ${each.key}')
  EOT
  rule {
    detect_label  = "High Failure Rate for ${each.key}"
    severity      = "Minor"
    notifications = var.notifications}
}
```

### 6.4 How This Applies to Tool Design

The tool should:
- Ship a library of **detector templates** (static threshold, anomaly, SLO burn-rate, dependency reliability)
- Accept high-level parameters (metric name, filter dimensions, threshold, severity) and render complete HCL
- Support `for_each` patterns for batch detector creation
- Validate that all required fields are populated before rendering

**Source**: [HOWTO: Create a SignalFX alert](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202045217eee26294e4a8b9722f57c2da123/pages/6266122391), [How To: Add New SignalFx Detectors in Terraform](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120204aa07fe7450f489899b60900ad6a0967/pages/5977304542)

