## 10. Shared `atlassian_ml_platform` Base Client Design Implications

### 10.1 Patterns to Extract from responsible-ai-api

| Pattern | How to Implement in Base Client |
|---------|---------------------------------|
| **Circuit Breaker** | Wrap all HTTP calls; open at 50% failure rate over 10-call window;10s recovery wait |
| **Kill Switch** | Check LaunchDarkly/Dynamic Config flag before every operation; if flag=off, return no-op |
| **Per-Tenant Rate Limit** | Use service context (tenant_id, user_id) to bucket API calls; Heimdall or local token bucket |
| **SignalFx Detector Definitions** | Standard IaC layout; tool generates HCL in `operations/terraform/` |
| **Retry with Backoff** | Exponential backoff on 429/503; max 3 retries |
| **Structured Logging** | Emit metrics for each API call (latency, status code, circuit breaker state) |
| **Token Caching** | sLauth tokens cached with refresh; personal tokens from env var |

### 10.2 Client Configuration Shape

```python
@dataclass
class AtlassianMLPlatformConfig:
    """Shared config for all ML platform API wrappers."""
    service_id: str               # Microscope service ID
    environment: str              # "prod" | "staging" | "ddev"
    terraform_path: str           # Relative path to .tf directory
    sauron_config_path: str       # Path to .sauron.yml
    
    # SignalFx-specific
    signalfx_realm: str = "us1"
    signalfx_team_id: str = ""
    signalfx_token_env_var: str = "SFX_TOKEN"
    
    # Resilience
    circuit_breaker_failure_threshold: float = 0.5
    circuit_breaker_window_size: int = 10
    circuit_breaker_wait_duration_seconds: int = 10
    rate_limit_per_minute: int = 50
    
    # Kill switch
    kill_switch_flag: str = "ml_platform_tools_enabled"
```

