## 8. Recommended Wrapper/Tool Shape for `signalfx_detector_client`

### 8.1 Minimum Command Surface

| Operation | Implementation | Human Confirmation Required? |
|-----------|---------------|------------------------------|
| `list_detectors(service_id, team_id)` | REST API GET `/v2/detector?name=...` | No (read-only) |
| `get_detector(detector_id)` | REST API GET `/v2/detector/{id}` | No (read-only) |
| `validate_signalflow(program_text)` | REST API POST `/v2/signalflow/preflight` | No (dry-run) |
| `author_detector_hcl(spec)` | Template rendering → HCL string | No (code gen only) |
| `apply_detector(tf_file_path)` | `sfm plan` → output plan → await approval | **Yes** (mutating) |
| `backtest_detector(program_text, start, stop)` | REST API POST `/v2/signalflow/execute` | No (read-only) |
| `import_detector(detector_id)` | `sfm import` or `terraform import` | **Yes** (state mutation) |
| `delete_detector(detector_id)` | `terraform destroy -target=...` | **Yes** (destructive) |

### 8.2 Auth/Config Pattern

```python
class SignalFxDetectorClient:
    """Base client for SignalFx detector operations."""
    
    def __init__(self, config: SignalFxConfig):
        self.realm = config.realm  # "us1"
        self.api_url = f"https://api.{self.realm}.signalfx.com"
        self.token = config.token  # From env var or sLauth
        self.service_id = config.service_id
        self.terraform_path = config.terraform_path  # "operations/terraform"
        # Circuit breaker: Resilience4j-style (from responsible-ai-api pattern)
    # Kill switch: check feature flag before each operation
    # Rate limit: max 50 API calls per minute per client instance
```

### 8.3 Detector Spec (Input to `author_detector_hcl`)

```python
@dataclass
class DetectorSpec:
    """High-level detector specification."""
    name: str                      # Human-readable name
    description: str               # What this monitors
    metric_name: str               # SignalFx metric name
    filters: Dict[str, str]        # dimension → value
    condition_type: str            # "threshold" | "anomaly" | "slo_burn_rate"
    threshold: Optional[float]     # For threshold detectors
    lasting: str = "5m"            # How long condition must persist
    severity: str = "Critical"     # Alert severity
    team_id: str = ""              # SignalFx team ID
    notifications: List[str] = []  # Opsgenie/Slack routing
    runbook_url: str = ""          # REQUIRED - runbook link
    environment: str = "prod"      # Environment filter
    resource_name_prefix: str = "" # Prefix for resource naming
```

### 8.4 Output: Generated HCL

The tool renders a complete `.tf` file that follows Atlassian conventions:

```hcl
resource "signalfx_detector" "${snake_case_name}" {
  name= "${var.resource_name_prefix}${spec.name}"
  description       = "${spec.description}"
  teams             = [var.signalfx_team_id]
  show_data_markers = true
  show_event_lines  = false

  program_text = <<-EOF
    A = data('${spec.metric_name}', 
             filter=${rendered_filters},
             rollup='sum')
        .sum()
        .publish(label='A')
    detect(when(A > threshold(${spec.threshold}), lasting='${spec.lasting}'))
      .publish('${spec.name}')
  EOF

  rule {
    detect_label          = "${spec.name}"
    severity              = "${spec.severity}"
    description           = "${spec.description}"
    notifications         = var.notifications
    runbook_url           = "${spec.runbook_url}"
    parameterized_subject = "{{ruleSeverity}} Alert: {{{ruleName}}} ({{{detectorName}}})"
  }
}
```

