## 9. CI/CD Workflow: Author → Apply Semantics

### 9.1 End-to-End Flow

```
AI Employee generates .tf file→ Writes to operations/terraform/detectors/<name>.tf
    → Commits to feature branch
    → Opens PR in Bitbucket
    → Bitbucket Pipeline runs Sauron (terraform plan)
    → Human reviews plan output
    → Merge to main
    → Sauron applies (terraform apply)
    → Detector appears in SignalFx
    → Verify in UI
```

### 9.2 Local Dev Loop (for validation)

```bash
cd operations/terraform
sfm init# Download plugins, validate config
sfm plan                    # Preview changes (dry-run)
sfm apply                   # Apply to test environment
sfm destroy -target='...'   # Clean up test detector
```

### 9.3 Backtesting Integration

From [Automating Detector Backtesting](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020d348e076907d4dc996757e397d745165/pages/6276133988):

```go
// Execute SignalFlow program against historical data
execReq := &signalflow.ExecuteRequest{
    Program: program,
    Start:   time.Now().Add(-7 * 24 * time.Hour),
    Stop:    time.Now().Add(-15 * time.Minute),  // 15-min data lag offset
}
```

Count firings as `ok → anomalous` state transitions.

