## 11. Best Practices for Tool/Skill Encoding

### 11.1 Workflow Steps (for SKILL.md)

1. **Identify metric** — Determine which SignalFx metric to monitor (from code instrumentation)
2. **Define filters** — Specify dimension filters (service_id, environment, endpoint)
3. **Choose detector type** — Static threshold, anomaly, SLO burn-rate
4. **Set thresholds** — Start conservative (above baseline noise), tighten after2weeks
5. **Configure routing** — OpsGenie team + Slack channel
6. **Attach runbook** — Every detector MUST have a runbook URL
7. **Generate HCL** — Render Terraform resource
8. **Validate** — `sfm plan` or `terraform plan` (dry-run)
9. **PR & Review** — Open PR, inspect plan output
10. **Merge & Apply** — Sauron applies on merge to main
11. **Verify** — Check detector exists in SignalFx UI

### 11.2 Where Human Confirmation is Required

- **Creating/updating/deleting detectors** (mutating production alerting)
- **Changing notification routing** (could page people incorrectly)
- **Importing existing detectors** (modifies Terraform state)
- **Adjusting thresholds on active detectors** (could cause alert storms)

### 11.3 Autonomous Execution OK

- Listing existing detectors (read-only)
- Validating SignalFlow programs (preflight)
- Generating HCL code (no side effects)
- Backtesting against historical data (read-only)
- Checking detector status

