## 5. Micros Service Deployment (Traditional Path)

### What it is
The traditional Micros PaaS deployment path relevant when TEAMServe services themselves need to be deployed as Micros services, or when the wrapper tool must interact with Micros-deployed services.

### Atlas CLI Commands (Minimum Command Surface)

```bash
# Deploy
atlas micros service deploy -s <service> -e <env> -f <sd.yml>

# Show status
atlas micros service show -s <service>

# Rollback
atlas micros service rollback -s <service> -e <env>

# Progressive rollout monitoring
atlas micros service rollout follow -s <service> -e <env>
atlas micros service rollout status -s <service> -e <env>

# Roll forward (canary → stable)
atlas micros service rollforward -s <service> -e <env> --target100

# View deployed descriptor
atlas micros service descriptor show -s <service> -e <env>

# Scale
atlas micros compute scale -s <service> -e <env> --desired=N

# Undeploy
atlas micros service undeploy -s <service> -e <env>
```

### Micros REST API (Programmatic)

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|--------|----------|---------|
| POST | `/api/v1/deployments_async/{service}/{env}` | Initiate async deployment |
| GET | `/api/v1/deployments_async/{service}/{env}/status/{operationId}` | Poll deployment status |
| Various | `/api/v1/deployments/{name}/{env}/{deploymentId}/scale` | Scale deployment |
| Various | `/api/v1/deployments/{name}/{env}/{deploymentId}/command` | Send command |

### Auth for Micros API
- **Slauth token** (human/CLI): `atlas slauth curl --aud micros-server --mfa -- -X GET<url>`
- **ASAP** (service-to-service): Audience = `micros-server`. Production services can make read/write calls.
- **Deploy tokens** (CI/CD): JWT from build server (Bamboo, Pipelines, Spinnaker)

### Service Descriptor (Minimum Valid)

```yaml
name: My Cool Service
organization: Engineering Services
notifications:
  email: user@atlassian.com
links:
  healthcheck:
    uri: /healthcheck
  source:
    url: <bitbucket-url>
compose:
  microservice:
    image: docker.atl-paas.net/atlassian/my-cool-service
    tag: 0.0.1
    ports:
    - 8080:8080
buildNumber: 0.0.1
```

### Deployment Modes

| Mode | Description | Duration | Notes |
|------|-------------|----------|-------|
| `cutover` | Blue/green default | ~10 min | DNS flip |
| `progressive` | **DEPRECATED** (use Spinnaker) | Variable | Gradual traffic shift |
| `hot-swap` | Code-only update | ~5 min | ddev/dev-west2 default |

### SignalFx Events on Deployment
- `Deployment completed`
- `Deployment Error`
- `Service rollback finished`
- `Service rollforward CONTINUE`
- `Service rollforward COMPLETE`

**Source**: [Upgrading an existing service](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MICROS/pages/167214365), [Micros Async Deployment API](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020ec0e248456e3455c981e199d722bef0f/blog/2025/06/10/5412016459), [HOWTO: Make authenticated requests to Micros HTTP API](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MICROS/pages/167214195)

