## 2. Production Deployment: Micros Service Descriptor

### What It Is
For production endpoints, SageMaker resources are declared in Micros service descriptors (`.sd.yml`). The SageMaker-OSB provider then provisions the endpoint via CloudFormation.

### Resource Types

| Resource Type | Use Case |
|--------------|----------|
| `sm-endpoint` | Single model, single container endpoint |
| `sm-mc-endpoint` | Multi-container endpoint (multiple models, different frameworks) |
| `sm-mm-endpoint` | Multi-model endpoint (multiple models, same container) |
| `sm-ic-endpoint` | Inference Components endpoint (independent scaling per model) |

### Service Descriptor Schema (§5.1 core)
```yaml
resources:
  - type: sm-endpoint
    name: my-cool-model
    attributes:
      # Required: Docker container image (AWS DLC or custom ECR)
      container: huggingface-pytorch-inference:2.0.0-transformers4.28.1-gpu-py310-cu118-ubuntu20.04
      
      # Required: Model artifact reference in Tarot (model_group/version_tag)
      artifact: _sox/my-model-group/v1
      
      # Optional: Environment variables for the container
      environment:
        HF_TASK: feature-extraction
        SAGEMAKER_PROGRAM: inference.py
        SAGEMAKER_SUBMIT_DIRECTORY: /opt/ml/model/code
      # Optional: Model data download timeout (for large models)
      modelDataDownloadTimeoutInSeconds: 3600
      
      # Required: Scaling configuration
      scaling:
        instance: ml.g5.xlarge      # SageMaker instance type
        min: 1                       # Minimum instances
        max: 3                       # Maximum instances
        threshold: 180# InvocationsPerInstance target (default: 180)
        cooldown: 300                # Seconds between scaling actions (default: 300)
      
      # Optional: CloudWatch alarms
      alarms:
        ModelLatencyHigh:
          MetricName: ModelLatency
          Namespace: AWS/SageMaker
          Threshold: 500000.0  # microseconds
          Priority: LowEvaluationPeriods: 3
          Period: 300
          ComparisonOperator: GreaterThanThreshold
          Statistic: Average
          Unit: Microseconds
```

### Inference Components Endpoint (newer, multi-model)
```yaml
- name: my-ic-endpoint
  type: sm-ic-endpoint
  attributes:
    components:
      - componentName: my-component-1
        containerImage: huggingface-pytorch-inference:2.0.0-transformers4.28.1-gpu-py310-cu118-ubuntu20.04
        package: a766b59c-8a55-4d4f-9a5a-029699656f8f:latest
        environment:
          HF_TASK: fill-mask
        resourceRequirements:
          minMemoryRequiredInMb: 1024
          numberOfCpuCoresRequired: 0.25
        scaling:
          copyCount: 1
    scaling:
      instance: ml.m5.large
      min: 1
      max: 1
```

### Environment Variable Injection
After deployment, the endpoint name is injected as:
```
SM_ENDPOINT_{RESOURCE_NAME_UPPERCASE_UNDERSCORED}_ENDPOINT_NAME
```
Example: resource named `my-endpoint` → `SM_ENDPOINT_MY_ENDPOINT_ENDPOINT_NAME`

**Source**: [SageMaker resource service descriptor reference](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/2626728343), [Introducing sm-endpoint](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MICROS/blog/2023/11/10/3087958792)

