## 1. The Official SDK: `atlassian-msp-sdk`

### What It Is
The `atlassian-msp-sdk` is Atlassian's official Python SDK for interacting with the Model Serving Platform. It provides programmatic access to the ML Registry (Tarot) and SageMaker endpoint lifecycle (via Launchpad and TEAMServe).

### Installation
```bash
pip install atlassian-msp-sdk
```
Available from Atlassian's internal Artifactory.

### Module Structure (Current v0.9+)
| Module | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `atlassian_msp_sdk.registry` / `atlassian_msp_sdk.ml_registry` | Model registration (Tarot V2/V3 APIs) |
| `atlassian_msp_sdk.launcher` | SageMaker endpoint deployment (Launchpad) |
| `atlassian_msp_sdk.clients.launchpad.endpoint_ts` | TEAMServe endpoint deployment |
| `atlassian_msp_sdk.msp` | Legacy client interface |

### Key SDK Operations

#### Registry Operations (maps to model lifecycle in §5.1)
```python
from atlassian_msp_sdk import ml_registry, registry

# Get/Create component (V3 API)
component = ml_registry.get_component("namespace.ComponentName")

# Upload artifact
model_artifact = component.upload_artifact_files_as_tar_with_data_labels(
    input_directories={model_dir: "."},
    attribution=Attribution.no_attribution(),
    classification=Classification.none_classification()
)

# Register version
version = component.create_version(
    description="Model v1",
    labels=[],
    artifacts=[model_artifact.id, descriptor_artifact.id]
)

# Legacy V2 API (still widely used)
registry.get_model_group(model_group_name="my-model")
tar_file = registry.package_and_upload(source_dir, model_group_name="my-model")
registry.create_model_version(
    model_group_name="my-model",
    model_version_tag="v1",
    package_name=tar_file,
    user_metadata={}
)
registry.get_model_version("my-model", model_version_tag="v1")
registry.get_latest_model_version("my-model")
registry.download_model_version("my-model", model_version_tag="v1")
```

#### Endpoint Deployment via Launchpad (dev/test, maps to §5.1)
```python
from atlassian_msp_sdk import launcher

# Deploy to SageMaker (Launchpad)
endpoint = launcher.launch(
    container="763104351884.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/huggingface-pytorch-inference:2.1.0-transformers4.37.0-gpu-py310-cu118-ubuntu20.04",
    model_group_name="my-model",
    model_version_tag="v1",
    instance_type="ml.g5.2xlarge"
)

# Invoke
result = endpoint.invoke({"inputs": ["vectorize this"]})

# Describe
endpoint.get_endpoint_details()
endpoint.info()  # Returns metrics + CloudWatch logs

# Cleanup
endpoint.delete()
```

#### TEAMServe Deployment (newer GPU-optimized path)
```python
from datetime import timedelta
from atlassian_msp_sdk.clients.launchpad.endpoint_ts import launch_to_teamserve

endpoint = launch_to_teamserve(
    component_ref="my-model-component",
    version_ref="v1.0.0",
    instance_type="g6e.xlarge",
    container="teamserve/nvidia/tritonserver:25.05-py3",
    time_to_live=timedelta(hours=2),
    container_args={"loadModel": "my_model_name"},
    timeout=timedelta(minutes=10)
)

response = endpoint.invoke(
    body={"inputs": [{"name": "input", "data": [1, 2, 3]}]},
    content_type="application/json"
)
endpoint.delete()
```

### Authentication Patterns

| Context | Auth Method | Details |
|---------|-------------|---------|
| Databricks notebooks | ASAP (via proxy) | `msp.auth.Databricks(proxy=..., scope='compliant-msp-secrets', issuer_key='MSP_PROD_ASAP_ISSUER', data_uri_key='MSP_PROD_ASAP_DATA_URI')` |
| Bitbucket Pipelines | ASAP (via pipe) | `msp.auth.Pipeline` |
| CLI (atlas) | SLAuth | `atlas slauth curl -a tarot -e prod` |
| Micros services | IAM (STS assume role) | Service role auto-attached by Micros; `sagemaker:InvokeEndpoint` permission |
| TEAMServe gRPC | ASAP JWT | `Authorization` header with ASAP token via `TeamservePlugin` |

**Source**: [MSP SDK API design](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~lnagy/pages/3576774077), [Evaluate auth options](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/1781408059)

