## 4. Monitoring & Observability (§11.1)

### CloudWatch Metrics Available
| Metric | Namespace | Use |
|--------|-----------|-----|
| `Invocations` | AWS/SageMaker | Request count |
| `InvocationsPerInstance` | AWS/SageMaker | For autoscaling target |
| `ModelLatency` | AWS/SageMaker | Inference time (μs) |
| `OverheadLatency` | AWS/SageMaker | SageMaker routing overhead |
| `Invocation4XXErrors` | AWS/SageMaker | Client errors |
| `Invocation5XXErrors` | AWS/SageMaker | Server errors |
| `CPUUtilization` | /aws/sagemaker/Endpoints | CPU % |
| `MemoryUtilization` | /aws/sagemaker/Endpoints | Memory % |
| `GPUUtilization` | /aws/sagemaker/Endpoints | GPU % |
| `DiskUtilization` | /aws/sagemaker/Endpoints | Disk % |

### Observability Stack Integration
- **SignalFx**: CloudWatch metrics forwarded; detectors defined for alerting
- **Splunk**: Container logs forwarded via `micros_<service-name>` index
- **ObsDeck**: Pre-built dashboards for SageMaker metrics
- **OpsGenie**: Alarm routing for Tier-2 support

### Default Alarms (auto-provisioned by SageMaker-OSB)
```yaml
alarms:
  Invocation5XXErrorsHigh:
    MetricName: Invocation5XXErrors
    Namespace: AWS/SageMaker
    Threshold: 100
    EvaluationPeriods: 3
    Period: 300  # 15 minEndpointCPUUtilizationHigh:
    MetricName: CPUUtilization
    Namespace: /aws/sagemaker/Endpoints
    Threshold: 80
    EvaluationPeriods: 2
    Period: 300
  EndpointGPUUtilizationHigh:
    MetricName: GPUUtilization
    Namespace: /aws/sagemaker/Endpoints
    Threshold: 80
    EvaluationPeriods: 2
    Period: 300
```

### Autoscaling Configuration
```yaml
scaling:
  min: 1
  max: 10
  instance: ml.g5.xlarge
  threshold: 180# InvocationsPerInstance target (default: 180)
  cooldown: 300       # Time between scaling actions (default: 300s)
  # OR separate scale-in/out:
  ScaleIn: 600        # Conservative scale-down
  ScaleOut: 120       # Aggressive scale-up
```

**Key considerations**:
- Autoscaling takes ~2minutes p50 (cooldown + SageMaker time + model spin-up)
- GPU instances may take hours to scale if capacity is scarce
- `InvocationsPerInstance` works well for uniform request sizes; use `CPUUtilization` or `ConcurrentRequestsPerModel` for variable workloads
- Threshold of 180 is the default; many production services use 100or lower for latency-sensitive workloads

**Source**: [SageMaker Resources Autoscaling guidelines](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~701211be51eacdbeb44df8a8fa56757a254d9/pages/3907418837), [RUNBOOK: SAGEMAKER: EndpointUtilizationHigh](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MICROS/pages/3306489233)

