## 5. Levels of Model Quality Verification (Three-Level Framework)

### What it is
A structured validation framework defining what must pass before production:

| Level | Name | What it Guarantees | Platform Verification |
|-------|------|-------------------|----------------------|
| 1 | Functional Correctness | Model boots, accepts request, returns expected output | Launchpad + ML Registry |
| 2 | Performance Under Load | Model handles expected throughput at acceptable latency | Launchpad load testing + perf_analyzer |
| 3 | Quality vs Baseline | Model delivers better results than existing production model | Offline evaluation (ML Studio) |

### How it applies to wrapper design
An AI employee tool wrapping Launchpad should support all three levels as distinct operations:
1. `validate_launch` — Level 1 (functional smoke test)
2. `validate_load` — Level 2 (performance benchmark)
3. `validate_quality` — Level 3 (offline eval, separate from Launchpad)

### Source
- [Levels of Model Quality and Platform Verification](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AO2/pages/6432265318)

