## 6. Mapping to §5.1 and §11.1 (Role-Doc Operations)

Based on the research, here's how Launchpad operations map to the referenced sections:

### §5.1 — Pre-Production Model Validation Operations

| Role-Doc Operation | SDK/API Call | Notes |
|-------------------|-------------|-------|
| Deploy model to pre-prod | `launchpad.launch_to_teamserve(...)` | Ephemeral K8s endpoint |
| Check deployment status | `endpoint.get_endpoint_details()` / `GET /status/{id}` | Poll until InService |
| Run smoke test inference | `endpoint.invoke(golden_request)` | Validate response shape |
| Run load test | `ts_lp_loadtest_validation` module / `benchmark.run_load_test(...)` | perf_analyzer or Locust |
| Record validation result | ML Registry annotation (`ts_launch_validation`) | Persistent audit trail |
| Cleanup endpoint | `endpoint.delete()` / `POST /destroy` | Also auto-cleaned via TTL |
| Check compliance | ML Registry + DMP gatekeeper validation | Artifact ARIs checked |

### §11.1 — Automated Validation Pipeline

| Role-Doc Operation | Implementation | Notes |
|-------------------|---------------|-------|
| Automated quality gate | ML Studio workflow with both modules | Sequential: launch → loadtest |
| Gate promotion on validation | Check for annotation presence in ML Registry | Promotion blocked without both annotations |
| CI/CD integration | Bitbucket Pipelines + MSP SDK | Spin up endpoint in pipeline, test, cleanup |
| Model registration | `atlas ml registry` CLI / MSP SDK | V3 API with compliance tracking |

