## 2. TEAMServe API — Backend REST API

### What it is
The `teamserve-api` service is a FastAPI-based control plane that manages model deployments on TEAMServe K8s clusters. It lives in the dev control plane cluster and orchestrates ephemeral model deployments via ArgoCD.

### API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|--------|----------|---------|
| POST | `/api/v1/model-deployment/launch` | Create deployment |
| PUT | `/api/v1/model-deployment/update` | Update model version (hot swap) |
| GET | `/api/v1/model-deployment/status/{id}` | Get live status |
| GET | `/api/v1/model-deployment/list` | List deployments |
| POST | `/api/v1/model-deployment/destroy` | Delete deployment |
| POST | `/api/v1/model-deployment/set-expiry/{id}` | Extend TTL |

**Model Invocation URL patterns:**
- Launchpad (dev): `https://<base-url>/v1/models/launchpad/mlp/versions/<model_version>/v2/models/<loadModel>/infer`
- For Triton: `/v2/models/<loadModel>/infer`
- For trtllm-serve/vLLM: `/v1/chat/completions`

### Auth Pattern
- **Launchpad → TEAMServe**: ASAP service-to-service authentication- Issuer: `micros/msp-sagemaker-launchpad`
  - Audience: `teamserve`
  - Token minting: `atlas asap key generate -k micros/msp-sagemaker-launchpad/$USER-test-key -a teamserve`
- **User → Launchpad**: SLAuth token (staff authentication via `atlas slauth token`)
- **SDK handles auth automatically** when running in Databricks/ML Studio environments

### Status Mapping (ArgoCD → API Status)

| ArgoCD Health | Sync Status | API Status | Action |
|--------------|-------------|------------|--------|
| Missing | Any | Creating | Wait |
| Progressing | Synced | Creating/Updating | Wait |
| Healthy | Synced | InService | ✅ Ready |
| Degraded | Any | Failed | Check logs |
| Any | OutOfSync | Updating | Wait |

### Deployment Strategy
- **Recreate** (not RollingUpdate) — single replica with exclusive GPU
- Flow: Terminate old pod → Wait (30s grace) → GPU freed → Schedule new pod → New model starts
- GPU reuse on same instance

