## 2. Auth/Config Pattern (Slauth/ASAP/IAM)

### What It Is
AI Gateway supports three authentication methods, with different trade-offs:

| Method | How It Works | Rate Limits | Use Case |
|---|---|---|---|
| **ASAP (Primary)** | Service→AI Gateway direct via ASAP JWT token | 20,000 RPM default (configurable) | Production services |
| **SLAuth** | Service→AI Gateway via SLAuth token | Same as ASAP | CLI tools, Bitbucket Pipelines |
| **Build Token** | Bitbucket Pipelines JWT (`PIPELINES_JWT_TOKEN`) | Backend-limited | CI/CD automated testing |

### Production Pattern (Micros Service with Egress Proxy)

The recommended production integration uses **service proxy egress**:

```yaml
# archetype-descriptor.yaml / service descriptor
serviceProxy:
  enabled: true
  egress:
    dependencies:
      - name: ai-gateway
        authentication:
          enabled: true
```

This injects `MESH_DEPENDENCY_AI_GATEWAY_BASE_URL` environment variable and auto-attaches ASAP credentials. The request then uses:
- Header: `'X-SLAuth-Egress': 'true'` (when using service proxy)
- Or: `Authorization: bearer <asap_token>` (direct ASAP)

### Required Headers (Every Request)

| Header | Purpose | Required? |
|---|---|---|
| `X-Atlassian-UseCaseId` | Identifies approved use case | **Yes** |
| `X-Atlassian-CloudId` | Tenant cloud ID (analytics/routing) | **Yes** |
| `User-Context` | UCT token (recommended for user identity) | **Recommended** |
| `Staff-Context` | SCT token (alternative for internal services) | Alternative |
| `X-Atlassian-UserId` | **DEPRECATED** — use UCT/SCT instead | Legacy only |

### Authorization Flow
1. Obtain a **use case ID** via the [AI Gateway onboarding form](go/mldesk) — requires privacy/legal approval
2. Register ASAP principal for the use case:
   ```shell
   atlas ml aigateway usecase auth add -i <use-case-id> -e prod-east -p <principal> -t ASAP_ISSUER
   ```
3. Wait5-10 minutes for propagation

### Local Development Auth (for testing)
```shell
# Install Slauth plugin
atlas plugin install -n slauth
# Start local Slauth server
atlas slauth server --port 5000
# Or use Lanyard proxy for ASAP token generation
```

**Source**: [AI Gateway Authentication Setup Guide](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120209092413fa40e489dbbb5fd1e58fa771b/pages/6332130515/AI+Gateway+Authentication+Setup+Guide), [AI Gateway Access](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/5795990861/AI+Gateway+Access), [Steps for integrating service with AI Gateway](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~639985befbf54baf2903aab8/pages/3700963654/Steps+for+integrating+service+with+AI+Gateway)

### How It Applies to Tool Design
For the `atlassian_ml_platform` base client:
- Use ASAP auth via service proxy egress (production) — auto-configured from `MESH_DEPENDENCY_AI_GATEWAY_BASE_URL`
- Support SLAuth for local dev / CLI invocation via `atlas slauth server`
- Inject `X-Atlassian-UseCaseId`, `X-Atlassian-CloudId`, and `User-Context` headers on every request
- The base client should abstract the auth mechanism behind a config interface, auto-detecting environment

