## §3.2 / §5.1 Mapping: Multi-Vendor LLM Routing via AI Gateway

---

## 1. Official SDK / Endpoint (Reuse > Rebuild)

### What It Is
The **AI Gateway SDK** (`atlassian-ai-gateway-sdk`) is a comprehensive monorepo providing multi-language SDKs (Java, Python, Node.js/TypeScript) that act as typed clients over vendor LLM APIs. It is the official, supported integration path for all Atlassian services calling LLMs.

**Package Names:**
- **Python**: `atlassian-ai-gateway-sdk` (also `atlassian_ml_studio_sdk` for high-level abstractions)
- **Java**: `com.atlassian.mlp:ai-gateway-sdk` (Maven)
- **Node.js**: `@atlassian/ai-gateway-sdk` (NPM via Atlassian registry)

**Repository**: Bitbucket — `ai-gateway-sdk` monorepo
- Source: [AI Gateway SDK Repository Analysis](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020403489a2707145929be398d28af8c052/pages/5687102084/AI+Gateway+SDK+Repository+Analysis)

### SDK v7 Client Types (Current — January 2026)
The SDK v7 introduced three tiers of client:

| Client Type | Description | Use Case |
|---|---|---|
| **Typed Client** | Strongly typed, validated DTOs from vendor swagger specs | Stable, critical production paths |
| **Generic Client** | Thin vendor-specific wrapper, no DTO validation | Fast-moving features, latest attributes |
| **Raw Client** | Direct HTTP/WebSocket access, no contract validation | Experimental endpoints, beta features |

**For AI Employee tool wrapper**: The **Generic Client** (thin wrapper) or **Raw Client** is recommended, as it provides maximum flexibility for an agent that needs to switch models dynamically without DTO rigidity.

**Source**: [Announcing AI Gateway SDK v7](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/blog/2026/01/27/6365279255/Announcing+AI+Gateway+SDK+v7+Clients+for+Every+Use+Case)

### API Endpoints

| API Version | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| **V1(Provider-Specific)** | `/v1/openai/v1/chat/completions` | Direct proxy to OpenAI-compatible format |
| **V1 (Provider-Specific)** | `/v1/google/v1/publishers/google/models/*` | Google Gemini via Vertex |
| **V1 (Provider-Specific)** | `/v1/bedrock/...` | AWS Bedrock (Claude, Nova, Llama) |
| **V2 (Unified)** | `/v2/chat` | Vendor-agnostic unified API with transformation |
| **V2 (Pass-Through)** | `/v2/invoke` | Pass-through with preferred/fallback model resolution |
| **V3 (Emerging)** | `/v3/chat` | Policy-aware with ARI-based content classification |

**Base URLs:**
- Production: `https://ai-gateway.prod-east.atl-paas.net`
- Staging: `https://ai-gateway.stg-east.atl-paas.net`

**Source**: [AI Gateway API Contract V2](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/5796018590/AI+Gateway+API+Contract+V2+Beta), [AI Gateway Access](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/5795990861/AI+Gateway+Access)

### How It Applies to Tool Design
The AI Employee wrapper should:
- **Reuse** `atlassian-ai-gateway-sdk` Python package (Generic Client mode) for production
- Target the **V2 Unified API** (`/v2/chat`) as the primary endpoint for model-agnostic routing
- Support fallback to V1 provider-specific endpoints when vendor-native features are needed
- Use the V2 `platform_attributes.routing` field (when M4 tier routing ships in Sept 2026) for tier-based routing

