## 3. Minimum Command Surface for Role-Doc Operations

### What the AI Employee Needs (§3.2— Model Invocation, §5.1 — Multi-Model Orchestration)

| Operation | API Path | SDK Method |
|---|---|---|
| **Chat completion (single-turn)** | `POST /v2/chat` | `unified.chat(request)` |
| **Streaming chat** | `POST /v2/chat` (with `stream: true`) | `unified.chat_stream(request)` |
| **Model-specific invocation** | `POST /v1/openai/v1/chat/completions` | `openai.v1ChatCompletions(request)` |
| **Pass-through invoke** | `POST /v2/invoke` | `raw.post("/v2/invoke", body)` |
| **Agentic tool-calling loop** | Multiple `POST /v2/chat` with tool results | Orchestrated via SDK |
| **Rate limit check** | CLI: `atlas ml aigateway usecase ratelimit view` | N/A (operational) |
| **View use case config** | CLI: `atlas ml aigateway usecase view` | N/A (operational) |

### Minimum Wrapper Surface for AI Employee

```python
class AIGatewayClient:
    """Minimum command surface for AI Employee LLM routing."""
    
    def chat(self, messages, model, **kwargs) -> ChatResponse:
        """Single-turn or multi-turn chat completion via V2 unified API."""
    def chat_stream(self, messages, model, **kwargs) -> AsyncIterator[StreamEvent]:
        """Streaming chat completion (SSE)."""
    
    def invoke_with_fallback(self, messages, preferred_model, fallback_model, **kwargs) -> InvokeResponse:
        """Pass-through invoke with automatic fallback."""
    
    def chat_with_tools(self, messages, tools, model, **kwargs) -> ChatResponse:
        """Tool-calling enabled chat (agentic loops)."""
```

