## 4. Request/Response Shapes and Rate-Limit Gotchas

### V2 Unified API Request Shape

```json
{
  "platform_attributes": {
    "model": "anthropic:claude-opus-4-6",
    "fallback": {
      "model": "gemini-3-flash-001",
      "strategy": "DEFAULT"  // DEFAULT | ENFORCED | NONE
    }
  },
  "request_payload": {
    "messages": [
      {"role": "system", "content": "..."},
      {"role": "user", "content": "..."}
    ],
    "temperature": 0.7,
    "max_tokens": 4096,
    "stream": false,
    "tools": [...],
    "tool_choice": "auto"
  },
  "additional_request_fields": {
    "model-id": {
      "$.json.path": "value"
    }
  },
  "additional_response_fields": {
    "model-id": ["$.path.to.extract"]
  }
}
```

### V2 Unified API Response Shape (Non-Streaming)

```json
{
  "additionalResponseFields": {},
  "metrics": {
    "vendor": "openai",
    "latencyMs": 1234,
    "usage": {
      "promptTokens": 150,
      "completionTokens": 200,
      "totalTokens": 350
    }
  },
  "output": [
    {
      "message": {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Hello! How can I help?",
        "toolCalls": null
      },
      "stopReason": "stop"
    }
  ]
}
```

### V2 Streaming Response (SSE)

```json
[{
  "additionalResponseFields": {},
  "metrics": {
    "vendor": "openai",
    "latencyMs": 234,
    "usage": {
      "promptTokens": 150,
      "completionTokens": 5,
      "totalTokens": 155
    }
  },
  "delta": [
    {
      "stopReason": null,
      "message": {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Hello",
        "toolCalls": null
      }
    }
  ]
}]
```

### Response Headers (Critical for Observability)

| Header | When Present | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `x-atlassian-serving-model` | Always | Model that actually served the request |
| `x-atlassian-requested-model` | When different from serving | Original model requested |
| `x-atlassian-model-routing-strategy` | On reroute | Why routing changed (e.g., `ahm-reroute`) |
| `x-ratelimit-limit` | On429 | Current rate limit value |
| `x-ratelimit-type` | On 429 | Which limit was hit (see below) |
| `retry-after` | On 429 | Seconds to wait |
| `x-ratelimit-reset` | On 429 | When limit resets |

### Rate-Limit Gotchas

**5 Rate Limit Types** (from `X-RateLimit-Type` header):

| Type | Scope | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `MODEL.USE_CASE` | Global per model family + use_case_id | TPM quota exhausted |
| `USER` | Per individual user (AAID) | Single user hogging capacity |
| `USE_CASE.MODEL.TENANT` | Per use_case + model + tenant (cloudId) | One tenant consuming all capacity |
| `USE_CASE.MODEL.USER` | Per use_case + model + user | Most granular limit |
| `UPSTREAM` | Vendor-returned429/529 | Provider capacity exhausted |

**Critical gotchas:**
1. **Default TPM quota is 100,000 tokens/min per use case + model family** — this is VERY low for agentic workloads
2. **Bursty traffic can burn the full minute budget in 1-2 seconds** — Heimdall currently uses minute-level windows
3. **Per-second burst limiting is shipping** (May 2026via Redis-backed token bucket) for AI Gateway
4. **No automatic retry on 429** — callers must implement their own backoff
5. **UPSTREAM 429 is different from gateway 429** — the vendor ran out of capacity vs. your quota is exhausted
6. **Heimdall config file is ~800KB** — scaling issues with 300-400+ use cases means occasional config propagation delays

**Rate Limit CLI Commands:**
```shell
# View current limits
atlas ml aigateway usecase ratelimit view -i <use-case-id> -e prod-east -m <model-id>

# Request increase (requires template + approval)
# See: https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6269871801
```

**Source**: [AI Gateway Rate Limiting](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/5796043394/AI+Gateway+Rate+Limiting), [AI Gateway Rate Limit Types](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/qura/pages/6750318615/AI+Gateway+Rate+Limit+Types+USER+vs+UPSTREAM), [RFC: Unified API Request and Response Body](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/4634032693/RFC+Unified+API+Request+and+Response+Body)

