## 7. Policy-Driven Model Routing (M1–M4) — Emerging Capability

### What It Is
The most significant AI Gateway architectural initiative (May–September 2026). Enables platform-controlled model switching without caller code changes.

### Canonical Model ID Format (M1 — June 2026)
```
provider:modelId
# Examples:
# anthropic:claude-opus-4-6
# openai:gpt-5.3
# google:gemini-3-flash
```

### Model Tiers (M4 — September 2026)
| Tier | Description | Example Models |
|---|---|---|
| `frontier` | Best-in-class reasoning | GPT-5.3, Claude Opus4.6 |
| `standard` | Balanced quality/cost | Claude Sonnet 4.5, Gemini 3Pro |
| `light` | Cost-optimized | GPT-4.1, Gemini 3Flash |

### Future-Proof Request Shape (After M4)
```json
{
  "platform_attributes": {
    "routing": {
      "tier": "STANDARD",
      "capability": "GENERAL",
      "preferred_model": "gpt-5.3"
    }
  },
  "request_payload": { "messages": [...] }
}
```

### How It Applies
The AI Employee wrapper should:
- Use canonical `provider:modelId` format today (M1 ready)
- Plan for `model_tier` field adoption when M4 ships
- Parse explainability response headers to log actual routing decisions
- Handle `X-Atlassian-Routing-Policy-Applied` to understand when platform overrode caller preference

**Source**: [AI Gateway — Policy-Driven Model Routing — Engineering Overview](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/7001278725/AI+Gateway+-+Policy-Driven+Model+Routing+-+Engineering+Overview), [Deep Research Report (May 2026)](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120203d68974c84a8453ab01c35740e7b4416/pages/7068910538/Atlassian+AI+Gateway+Deep+Research+Report+May+2026)

