## 2. `rovo_eval_runner` — Surface A: Assistance-Service-Eval (ASE / Rovoeval)

### What It Is
- **Service name**: `assistance-service-eval`
- **Compass component**: Active, Tier3
- **Platform**: Kotlin microservice on Micros
- **Purpose**: Centralized evaluation platform for Rovo Chat quality (online eval, daily eval, on-demand eval)
- **Scale**: ~55 runs/day, 50+ developers, ~175 specialized metrics, processes 100% live traffic
- **Cost**: ~$3.6M/year (inference spend for LLM judges)
- **Status**: Legacy/maintenance mode for new eval work (Stratus Evals SDK recommended instead)

### Execution Surface & API
- **UI Portal**: `go/rovoeval` — experiment creation, dataset management, results
- **Bot account**: `srca-ilr-bot@atlassian.com` (AAID: `712020:2b930393-8024-4b3f-96f6-7bad72b50ec6`)
- **Experiment model**: Feature flag-gated with `evaluationFeatureFlag` custom field
- **Architecture**: ConvoAI makes fire-and-forget HTTP POST to ASE after every turn; ASE runs LLM judge synchronously

### Key Interfaces
- `EvaluationContextFactory` — Creates product-specific execution contexts
- `RovoEvaluationContextFactory` — Sets up Rovo workspace context
- Calculators: Resolution rate, Plugin Invocation, Groundedness, Instruction Following, Abstain Detection, CSR v4

### Auth Pattern
- Bot API tokens (rotated every 90 days)
- Micros stash secrets: `atlas micros stash set --service=assistance-service-eval --env=prod-east --key=<KEY> --value=<VALUE>`
- Requires JIT access for config changes

