## 3. `rovo_eval_runner` — Surface B: Stratus Evals SDK (Recommended for New Work)

### What It Is
- **Package**: `atlassian-stratus-evals-sdk` (pip) / `stratus-evals` (Atlas plugin)
- **Repository**: `atlassian/stratus-evals-sdk`
- **Language**: Python 3.12+, Go (CLI wrapper)
- **Version**: v0.9.0 (as of 2026-05-20)
- **Primary contributor**: Hrayr Matevosyan
- **Status**: Active, recommended for ALL new eval work

### Execution Surface & API

#### Agent Clients
| Client | Use Case | Init Command |
|--------|----------|--------------|
| **ACP** | Any ACP-compatible agent (Atlas Alta, etc.) | `stratus_evals init --client acp` |
| **A2A** | Any A2A HTTP endpoint including ConvoAI | `stratus_evals init --client a2a` |
| **Convo AI** | Rovo agents on Convo-AI platform | `stratus_evals init --client convo_ai` |
| **AI Gateway LLM** | Direct LLM baseline / model comparison | `stratus_evals init --client ai_gateway_llm` |

#### CLI Commands
```bash
# Install
pip install atlassian-stratus-evals-sdk
# or
atlas plugin install -n stratus-evals

# Initialize
stratus_evals init --client convo_ai

# Run evaluation
stratus_evals eval ./datasets/my_dataset.json

# Validate config
stratus_evals validate

# Upload dataset
stratus_evals upload-dataset <path>
```

#### Dataset Format
```json
[
  {
    "task_id": "compaction_01",
    "query": "Search for information about how to setup a chatbot",
    "gt_answer": "A summary of chatbot setup approaches",
    "context": {},
    "expected_actions": ["EnterpriseSearch", "read_file"],
    "expected_plugins": [],
    "additional_fields": {}
  }
]
```

#### Configuration (secrets.env)
```env
CONVO_AI__BASE_URL=<url>
CONVO_AI__USER_NAME=test@atlassian.com
CONVO_AI__API_KEY=***
CONVO_AI__CLOUD_ID=<cloud_id>
CONVO_AI__USER_ID=<user_id>
```

### Architecture Flow
```
Dataset (JSON/JSONL/CSV) → stratus-evals-sdk → Agent Client → 
  [ConvoAI / A2A / AI Gateway LLM] → LLM Judge (via AI Gateway) → 
  Metrics (Accuracy, Latency, Tool Precision/Recall) → 
  [Local Results + Databricks/MLflow]
```

### Key Capabilities
- Multi-turn conversation support
- Tool invocation tracking (precision, recall, false-discovery rate)
- LLM-as-a-judge with customizable judge prompts
- HTML self-contained reports
- Databricks/MLflow tracking
- Bitbucket CI pipeline integration
- <10min onboarding

