## 2. Authentication Patterns (from Databricks at Atlassian)

### 2.1 Three Auth Methods Used Internally

| Method | When Used | How |
|--------|-----------|-----|
| **ASAP (JWT)** | Service-to-service from Databricks notebooks to internal services (IAS, ML Studio Orchestrator) | `atlassian_jwt_auth.create_signer(issuer, key_id, private_key)` → signed JWT with audience claim |
| **Databricks Bearer Token** | API calls to Databricks from outside (Micros services, Pipelines) | `Authorization: Bearer ${DATABRICKS_API_TOKEN_<workspace_id>}` stored in Micros stash |
| **Databricks OAuth (M2M / U2M)** | Local development, Socrates MCP | `databricks auth login --host <workspace>` → token stored in `~/.databrickscfg` |

### 2.2 ASAP Usage from Databricks

From [Identity - ASAP Token from Databricks](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/I/pages/3871446072):
- **Key finding**: "There is no Slauth token in the databricks environment variables" — ASAP is the standard auth from notebooks
- ASAP keys are stored as Databricks secrets: `dbutils.secrets.get(scope='<scope>', key='<key-name>')`
- Pattern: Generate ASAP token in notebook, use as Bearer for internal service calls

```python
import atlassian_jwt_auth

ASAP_KEY = dbutils.secrets.get(scope='my-scope', key='asap-private-key').replace("\\n", "\n")
signer = atlassian_jwt_auth.create_signer(ISSUER, ASAP_KEY_ID, ASAP_KEY)
asap_token = signer.generate_jwt(AUDIENCE)
headers = {"Authorization": f"Bearer {asap_token.decode('utf-8')}"}
```

### 2.3 Service-to-Databricks Auth (from Micros/PCP)

From [PCP Paimon Migration](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~792771592/pages/7062493109):
- Pattern: `DATABRICKS_API_TOKEN_{workspaceId}` stored as Micros stash variables
- `DatabricksApiClient.callDatabricksApi()` auto-adds `Authorization: Bearer $token`
- Tokens exist for all workspaces across all environments

**How it applies for AI employee**: Use Databricks Bearer token (stored in secrets) for programmatic notebook submission. ASAP for callbacks to internal services from within the notebook.

