## 8. ML Platform Service Landscape (What the Wrappers Need to Cover)

### Finding: Complete ML Platform Service Map

**What it is**: Atlassian's ML Platform consists of these key services that wrapper tools need to interface with:

| Service | Protocol | Auth | SDK/Client |
|---------|----------|------|------------|
| **AI Gateway** | REST (OpenAI-compatible) | ASAP/SLAuth-Egress | `atlassian-ai-gateway-sdk` (Python, Java, Node) |
| **Tecton/MLFS** | REST (Java SDK wraps) | ASAP | `com.atlassian.mlp.featurestore:java-client-sdk` (migrating) |
| **MLflow** | REST | Databricks auth | `mlflow` Python SDK |
| **ML Registry (Tarot v3)** | REST (atlas CLI) | ASAP/SLAuth | `atlassian-msp-sdk` |
| **TeamServe** | gRPC (Triton) | ASAP JWT | `tritonclient[grpc]`, custom `TeamservePlugin` |
| **SageMaker** | boto3 (AWS SDK) | IAM (AWS) | `boto3` |
| **ML Studio** | REST | ASAP | `atlassian-ml-studio-sdk` |
| **SignalFx** | REST | API token | Terraform provider / `signalfm` CLI |
| **Statsig** | REST/SDK | Server-secret | `atlassian-statsig-proxy` |

**How it applies**: The base client must be protocol-agnostic enough to support both REST and gRPC downstream calls, with pluggable auth strategies.

**Source**: [ML Platforms @ Atlassian](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020f8645f9b46414d32962ab94d66c30436/pages/6068577839), [End-to-End ML Framework @ Atlassian](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202046686c7c93274f379403a2283d58293f/pages/6708596091), [MLFS SDK adoption](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6721137225)

