## 12. MLFS/Tecton Feature Store Client Pattern

### Finding: MLFS SDK Migration from Tecton

**What it is**: Atlassian is migrating from Tecton (third-party) to MLFS (in-house feature store). The Java SDK (`com.atlassian.mlp.featurestore:java-client-sdk`) provides feature reads.

**How it works**:
```java
// Tecton SDK pattern (being deprecated)
FeatureServiceClient client = clientFactory.createFeatureServiceClient(featureServiceName, workspace).get();
CompletableFuture<Optional<List<Feature>>> result = client.getFeaturesFuture(joinKeys, requestContext, false);

// MLFS SDK (replacement) - same interface
implementation("com.atlassian.mlp.featurestore:java-client-sdk:0.0.36")
```

**Key constraints**:
- MLFS reads pass through Service Proxy (<10ms overhead)
- Latency challenge: Tecton reads directly from DynamoDB vs MLFS through additional hops
- Feature flag guards recommended for migration

**How it applies**: A Python MLFS wrapper would use the REST API (no Python SDK yet exists), inheriting the base client's retry/circuit-breaker patterns.

**Source**: [MLFS SDK adoption: migrate from Tecton SDK](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6721137225), [PSA: ML Platform is deprecating Tecton](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/blog/2025/12/03/6159139910)

