## 11. MLflow Run Convention Pattern

### Finding: Standard MLflow Usage at Atlassian

**What it is**: MLflow is used via `atlassian_ml_studio_sdk.ml_flow` package for experiment tracking with standardized naming conventions.

**How it works**:
- Experiment names encode: team, use case, dataset version
- Runs log: metrics (`mlflow.log_metric`), parameters (`mlflow.log_param`), artifacts (`mlflow.log_artifact`)
- Model artifacts addressed via `runs:/<run_id>/model`
- Registration: Models promoted via MSP SDK from MLflow run to ML Registry (Tarot v3)

**How it applies**: An MLflow wrapper tool would inherit the base client's auth/retry/logging but use the MLflow Python SDK directly, configured with appropriate tracking URIs.

**Source**: [End-to-End ML Framework @ Atlassian](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202046686c7c93274f379403a2283d58293f/pages/6708596091), [MLflow Integration in Airlock Flows](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/xugc/pages/6659921772), [An abridged guide for MLflow](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/1691633396)

