# Research Findings: responsible-ai-api Production Patterns for AI Employee Tool Design

## 1. Service Architecture Overview

### What it is
The `responsible-ai-api` (repo: `atlassian/responsible-ai-api`) is an Atlassian-internal **Tier-1** content-moderation microservice that provides AI safety capabilities including text-based AUP (Acceptable Use Policy) violation detection and AI agent filtering.

### Technical Profile
| Attribute | Details |
|-----------|---------|
| **Language** | Python |
| **Runtime** | gevent (async worker pool) |
| **Inference Client** | `tritonclient[grpc]2.56.0`, Custom `GrpcEndpoint` wrapper |
| **Model Connection** | gRPC with SSL/TLS to NVIDIA Triton via Teamserve |
| **HTTP Client** | `httpx` (for AI Gateway calls in agent moderation) |
| **Authentication** | ASAP JWT tokens in Authorization header |
| **Auth Plugin** | Custom `TeamservePlugin` for Teamserve auth |
| **Deployment** | Micros (AWS), ASG min:22instances, m6a.xlarge |
| **Multi-region** | responsible-ai-api (AWS us-east-1), responsible-ai-api-gcp |
| **Compass Tier** | 1 (highest) |

### API Surface —4 Moderation Endpoints
| Endpoint | Purpose | Downstream |
|----------|---------|------------|
| `POST /v1/moderation/prompt/` | Text prompt moderation | Teamserve (Triton gRPC) |
| `POST /v1/moderation/image/` | Image content moderation | SageMaker endpoint |
| `POST /v1/moderation/agent/` | Agent configuration moderation | AI Gateway (httpx) |
| `POST /v1/moderation/output/` | Output moderation (streaming) | Teamserve (Triton gRPC) |

All endpoints emit `ALLOWED/DISALLOWED` decisions with harm categories and confidence scores.

