### Current State (from AI-262, AI-248)
| Gap | Status | Priority |
|-----|--------|----------|
| 0 SignalFx detectors in IaC | Open | Critical |
| No per-endpoint SLOs encoded | Open | Critical |
| Agent endpoint fail-closed | Proposed fix (AI-266) | Critical |
| No per-tenant rate limit on /image | Proposed (AI-263) | High |
| gevent↔ blocking-gRPC pathology | 4SEV-2 incidents in 30 days | Critical |
| Primary runbook ~470 days stale | Updated2026-05-21 | Medium (now addressed) |
| OTel sidecar race on canary deploy | Known issue | High |

### Incident Pattern Summary (last 30 days)
From the AI-native SDLC page:
- 8HOT tickets in 30 days
- **Dominant root cause**: Teamserve latency/crashes → gevent thread exhaustion → cascading 5xx
- **Resolution pattern**: Most incidents "should be fixed by fail-open" once kill switches are activated
- **Current first-response**: Manual on-call triage via Splunk/SignalFx → atlas micros commands

