Report written to: …/worker_2/children/worker_6/outputs/facet.md


                              Headline Findings

 1 ORBIT has NO external write API. It's a read-side personalization layer
   that consumes pre-computed signals from Teamwork Graph (TwG) and the
   Context-Graph Relevance Layer (GRE). Writes flow in via connector 
   ingestion, not via a public mutator. The threat-model page explicitly
   states the Rovo TwG plugin "does not support writes except from connector
   ingestion."
    • Four practical write channels were identified for orbit_context_writer:
       1 TwG connector ingestion (long-term canonical; needs SLAuth +
         registered identity)
       2 Distilled-Knowledge ERS write (ati:cloud:convo-ai:distilled-knowledge
         v1, hashed on projectAri + agentId) — the direct AI-agent precedent
       3 Confluence-page mirror under an "ORBIT Memory" parent via
         mcp__atlassian__update_confluence_page (day-zero shim — recommended
         for v1)
       4 Jira-issue field write for issue-scoped enrichment
    • Net-new semantics layer required: extended distilled-knowledge envelope,
      4-strategy merge (dedup/contradiction/strengthening/consolidation),
      WRITE/SUPPRESS gates, hierarchy-of-truth precedence (human corrections
      always win), Tier-3→Tier-4 "golden plan" promotion.
 2 FinOps query plane is uniformly Socrates-SQL (Databricks Spark SQL) and is
   fully reachable via the already-available mcp__socrates MCP. No new 
   transport is needed for cost_attribution_query — only typed query templates
   + calibrated-uncertainty rendering.
    • Canonical tables:
      production.cloud_finops_ias.moi_cost_attribution_result_platform
      (primary), …result_product, metric_of_interest_deduped,
      production.cloud_finops_aws_cur.aws_focus_billing_data,
      production.cloud_finops_databricks.*, production.de_ai_linter.* (in
      flight), production.finance_fpa_anaplan.*.
    • Required cost-allocation tags identified (business_unit, service_name,
      resource_owner, service_uuid, dimension_1, dimension_2 — the latter is
      the per-experiment hook).
    • Four templated query patterns specified with concrete SQL:
      per-experiment rollup, per-team burn vs. R4F forecast,
      SageMaker→TEAMServe savings estimator (3-step with empirical 0.4916
      effective/list ratio), and anomaly-detection 4-check ensemble (replays
      the existing DailyFinOps Cost Anomaly Bot, page 5656283815).
    • Severity matrix: Sev 3 > $8K/wk cost spike, Sev 2 > $40K/wk; 2AF policy
      fires at > $50K/mo for 2 consecutive months.


