## Original User Request
**Description**: Create the GOVERNANCE, COMMUNICATION, and COST STEWARDSHIP toolkit — tools and skills for AI MLE responsibilities #9 (stakeholder communication) and #10 (cost & capacity stewardship), plus the cross-cutting governance/oversight surface (§7 collaboration, §8 KPIs reporting, §9 challenges, §10.5 guardrails, §11 day-one readiness). Candidate tools: deployment_manifest_generator (produce the §10.5 non-negotiable manifest: intent, non-goals, services/files, invariants, risk class, test plan, rollback plan, post-deploy monitoring plan), pir_auto_drafter (draft PIR within 5 BD from reasoning traces — TTD/TTH/TTR/TTC, gaps, prevention, playbook updates per §6 SOP-3 + §4.1), weekly_experiment_digest (auto-generated stakeholder digest from MLflow/ML Lens/registry events — §7.3), autonomy_tier_router (classify proposed action into 🟢/🟡/🔴 per Symphony 3-tier; gate execution — §10.5), policy_compliance_checker (verify proposed change against version-controlled policy pack: RFC-002, AI SDLC Policy — §10.5), orbit_context_writer (append experiments/incidents/decisions to ORBIT — §1, §10.4), cost_attribution_query (FinOps + ML Artifact Cost Monitoring queries, per-experiment budget enforcement, SageMaker→TEAMServe savings estimator — §2 #10, §5.3, §9), escalation_router (emit 🟡/🔴 packets to Human MLE Manager via Slack/Jira with full reasoning trace — §7.1), calibrated_uncertainty_reporter (format recommendations with confidence bounds, measured-vs-inferred separation, explicit 'I don't know' markers — §3.4, §10.5). Candidate skills: symphony-autonomy-policy (3-tier + L1–L5 maturity, tier-selection guidance, escalation rules — §10.5), deployment-manifest-authoring (§10.5), pir-drafting (§4.1, §6 SOP-3), stakeholder-communication-cadence (continuous/per-experiment/per-incident/daily/weekly/quarterly outputs as byproducts of work — §7.3), cost-stewardship (when/how to recommend infra migrations, budget anomaly response — §2 #10), orbit-enrichment (cumulative learning discipline; what to capture per task — §1, §10.4), day-one-readiness-bootstrap (§11 checklist: doc ingestion list, first-tasks sequence, L1/L2→L3 promotion gate). Justify why existing tools are insufficient: atlassian (Jira/Confluence) and slack MCPs provide delivery channels but not the governance/policy classification, manifest authoring, calibrated-uncertainty formatting, ORBIT write semantics, or FinOps queries that the role requires — these must be net-new.

**Todos**:
- RESEARCH FIRST: discover existing Atlassian governance artifacts (RFC-002, AI SDLC Policy, AIF L3-O1-KR1), Symphony Orchestrator API surface, ORBIT context-layer write paths, FinOps/ML Artifact Cost Monitoring data sources, and any existing Confluence templates for PIR/model card/runbook
- Determine whether existing atlassian + slack MCPs (from Subtask 1) suffice as delivery transport for PIR/digest/escalation, or whether thin wrapper tools are needed for templated rendering
- Design and create the manifest/pir/digest/escalation tools so they emit structured artifacts that reuse atlassian and slack MCPs for delivery
- Design the autonomy_tier_router and policy_compliance_checker tools so EVERY autonomous action passes through tier classification + policy check before execution
- Design the orbit_context_writer to be invoked at the end of every completed work item (enforces the 'never solves the same problem twice' principle)
- Create the symphony-autonomy-policy, stakeholder-communication-cadence, cost-stewardship, orbit-enrichment, and day-one-readiness-bootstrap skills with SKILL.md citing the role-doc sections that drive each guideline
- Ensure calibrated-uncertainty discipline (confidence bounds, measured-vs-inferred, explicit 'I don't know') is enforced by the calibrated_uncertainty_reporter tool and referenced from comms skills
</UserRequest>

