### 4.4 Cross-Cutting Concerns (Built into Base Client)

| Concern | Implementation | Source Pattern |
|---------|---------------|----------------|
| **Auth** | `ASAPAuthProvider` — caches tokens, auto-refreshes before expiry | responsible-ai-api ASAP headers |
| **Circuit Breaker** | Per-downstream, `fail_max=30`, half-open after 60s | responsible-ai-api `triton_circuit_breaker` |
| **Kill Switch** | Statsig feature gates checked before every call | RAI feature gates (`rai_enable_*`) |
| **Rate Limiting** | Client-side awareness via Hofund sidecar + backoff on429 | Convo-AI Heimdall integration |
| **Retry** | Exponential backoff with jitter; respect `retry-after` header | AI Gateway 429 handling |
| **Observability** | SignalFx metrics + OpenTelemetry spans | RAI service SignalFx integration |
| **Timeout** | Per-downstream configurable timeouts (6s for TeamServe, 30s for AI Gateway) | RAI service timeout patterns |

---

## 5. Rate Limit Gotchas & Error Patterns
**[Satisfies: Request/Response shapes, rate-limit gotchas]**

| Platform | Rate Limit Mechanism | Key Gotchas |
|----------|---------------------|-------------|
| **AI Gateway** | Heimdall (TPM-based per use-case × model) | Shared across all tenants per use case; vendor-side capacity is unknown and variable;429 with `retry-after` header |
| **TeamServe** | Capacity-limited (GPU bound) | `DEADLINE_EXCEEDED` on overload; `429Too Many Requests` from upstream; Triton `INTERNAL` errors on CUDA crashes |
| **MSP/Tarot** | Standard Micros rate limiting | Deploy operations can take 5-10min; S3 upload parallelism matters for large models |
| **MLFS** | ERS quota + Skybridge cache | DynamoDB throttling on high write rates; SQS pipeline backpressure |
| **Databricks/MLflow** | Workspace-level quotas | Large artifact downloads may fail; use chunked downloads |

**Error response patterns from RAI (reference):**
- `gRPC DEADLINE_EXCEEDED` → TeamServe too slow
- `429 Too Many Requests` → Upstream rate-limiting
- `Read timed out` (6s) → TeamServe slow/down
- `InferenceServerException: INTERNAL` → Triton/CUDA failure
- `API Exception` → Generic upstream error

