    ml-experiment-lifecycle, production-ml-incident-response,
    ml-evaluation-protocol, feature-store-hygiene, ml-runbook-authoring,
    ml-launch-review-checklist, model-card-and-architecture-comparison,
    hyperparameter-optimization-to-convergence, mlflow-run-conventions.
  5 Elevated AI-native standards encoded as non-negotiable gates in
    ml-evaluation-protocol: multi-seed N≥3 (N=5 for launch), K≥5 k-fold,
    mandatory slice axes (tenant/region/language/length/demographic),
    calibration ECE≤0.05, fairness gap threshold 0.05 → 🟡 escalation, ≥100
    failures per slice into ≥5 named buckets, mandatory ablations (missing =
    hard fail), HPO convergence proof (EI<ε for K consecutive trials),
    pre-registration before any training.
  6 Artifact template HTML scaffolds delivered for ML Runbook, Model Card,
    Architecture Comparison Report, and Launch Review Checklist — all in
    Confluence-compatible Rovo-Dev HTML with placeholders.
  7 Cross-tool integration patterns documented: Atlassian-as-substrate /
