## Original User Request
**Description**: Create the ML LIFECYCLE EXECUTION toolkit — the tools and skills that power AI MLE responsibilities #1–#8 (production model health, experiment lifecycle, training pipelines, feature engineering, packaging/registration, deployment/rollout, ML reliability engineering, evaluation/quality gating). Candidate tools (research-and-implement; many likely have Atlassian internal SDKs to wrap rather than rebuild): ml_studio_client (training job submit/inspect — driven by §2 #3, §5.1, §6 SOP-1), mlflow_client (run logging/query, model registration — §4.3 MLflow run pattern), tarot_registry_client (ML Registry v3 read/write, lineage, compliance metadata — §2 #5), tecton_mlfs_client (feature CRUD, freshness/coverage, online/offline consistency — §2 #4, §4.3), ml_lens_client (drift KS/KL/cosine, data-quality, model-perf, system-health queries + alert authoring — §2 #1, §4.3, §9), signalfx_detector_iac (detectors/SLOs as code — §2 #7, §5.3), teamserve_deploy_client (Micros service descriptors, canary/shadow control, rollback — §2 #6, §5.3), sagemaker_endpoint_client (owned endpoints — §5.1, §11.1), ai_gateway_routing_client (multi-vendor LLM routing — §3.2, §5.1), launchpad_validate (pre-prod model validation — §5.1, §11.1), rovo_eval_runner and aix_eval_runner (eval workflow execution — §4.2), databricks_notebook_runner (§5.1), responsible_ai_api_ops (rate-limiter inspect, circuit-breaker state, kill-switch toggles for the reference codebase — §5.3). Candidate skills: ml-experiment-lifecycle (SOP-2 hypothesis→parallel variants→ablations→error analysis→architecture comparison report), drift-triggered-retraining (SOP-1), production-ml-incident-response (SOP-3 circuit-breaker + cross-correlation + PIR draft handoff), ml-evaluation-protocol (6-stage with elevated AI-native standards: multi-seed, k-fold, slicing, calibration, fairness, exhaustive failure-case categorization — §4.2 + §10.2), feature-store-hygiene (proactive data-quality audit per connector/region/tenant — §10.4 + §11.3 task 4), ml-runbook-authoring (renders the [Template] ML Runbook — §4.1), ml-launch-review-checklist (automated gate enforcement — §4.1), model-card-and-architecture-comparison (artifact generation — §4.4), hyperparameter-optimization-to-convergence (Optimus Prime / Bayesian with statistical convergence verification — §10.2), mlflow-run-conventions (standardized run name, flattened params, per-segment metrics — §4.3). Justify why existing tools (from Subtask 1) are insufficient: existing MCP toolsets cover Atlassian collaboration surfaces and bitbucket SCM, but none expose ML Studio, MLflow, Tarot v3, Tecton/MLFS, ML Lens, SignalFx, TEAMServe, SageMaker, AI Gateway, or Launchpad APIs — all are platform-specific and required by the role's daily core loop.

**Todos**:
- RESEARCH FIRST: discover Atlassian internal Python SDKs / CLIs / API surfaces for ML Studio, Tarot v3 (ML Registry), Tecton/MLFS, ML Lens, SignalFx, TEAMServe, SageMaker, AI Gateway, Launchpad — reuse beats reimplement
- Examine the responsible-ai-api codebase as reference for production patterns and any reusable helper libraries (circuit breaker, kill-switch, per-tenant rate limit, SignalFx detector definitions)
- Design and create the ML Platform API-wrapper tools listed above with consistent auth/config (likely a shared 'atlassian_ml_platform' client base)
- Design and create the SOP-encoding skills (drift-triggered-retraining, experiment-lifecycle, incident-response, evaluation-protocol) with SKILL.md tying tool calls to the role-doc steps
- Encode elevated AI-native standards (multi-seed, k-fold, slicing, calibration, fairness, exhaustive failure-case categorization, mandatory ablations) into the ml-evaluation-protocol skill so they are non-negotiable
- Create artifact-generation skills/tools for the [Template] ML Runbook, ML Launch Review Checklist, Model Card, and Architecture Comparison Report
- Cross-reference each created capability back to its driving role-doc section (§2/§4/§5/§6/§10) for traceability
